{"retcode":0,"message":"OK","data":{"post":{"post":{"game_id":2,"post_id":"46233468","f_forum_id":0,"uid":"1015537","subject":"\"Everwinter Without Mercy\" Version 7.0 Update Details","content":"\u003cdiv class=\"ql-image img-center 710c8888-e1b0-4da6-84a1-f897cef27d29\" data-uuid=\"710c8888-e1b0-4da6-84a1-f897cef27d29\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"ql-image-wrp\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"ql-image-mask-wrapper\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://hoyolab-upload-private.hoyolab.com/upload/2026/08/11/0/bce0963941ee2f288f37d8153053d04c_8351898936364171162.jpeg?x-oss-process=image%2Fresize%2Cs_1000%2Fauto-orient%2C0%2Finterlace%2C1%2Fformat%2Cwebp%2Fquality%2Cq_70\" alt=\"\" align=\"img-center\" data-uuid=\"710c8888-e1b0-4da6-84a1-f897cef27d29\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"ql-image-desc-wrp\"\u003e\u003cp contenteditable=\"false\" class=\"ql-image-desc\" data-placeholder=\"Click to enter image description (up to 90 characters)\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDear Traveler,\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eBelow are the details of the Version 7.0 update \"Everwinter Without Mercy\" and the update compensation.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e〓Compensation Details〓\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eMaintenance Compensation: Primogems ×300 (60 Primogems per hour the servers are down)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIssue Fix Compensation: Primogems ×300 (please refer to the relevant compensation mail for more details)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e〓Scope of Compensation〓\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eMaintenance Compensation: Travelers who have reached Adventure Rank 5 or above by 2026/08/12 06:00 (UTC+8).\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eCompensation must be claimed before the end of Version 7.0.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIssue Fix Compensation: Travelers who have reached Adventure Rank 5 or above by 2026/08/12 06:00 (UTC+8).\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePlease log in and claim your compensation before 2026/08/15 06:00 (UTC+8).\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eOur developers will distribute compensation to Travelers via in-game mail within 5 hours after the update maintenance is finished. The mail will expire after 30 days, so don't forget to claim the attached compensation in time.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e〓Update Schedule〓\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eUpdate maintenance begins 2026/08/12 06:00 (UTC+8) and is estimated to take 5 hours.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e〓How to Update Game Client〓\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePC: Close the game, open the Genshin Impact Launcher, and click Update.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eiOS: Open the App Store and tap Update.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAndroid: Open the game and follow the directions on-screen.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePlayStation®: Highlight \"Genshin Impact\" from the Home screen, press the OPTIONS button and select \"Check for Update.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eXbox Series X|S: Open the system main menu, select \"My games \u0026amp; apps,\" select the \"Manage\" tab, and on the \"Updates\" page, find \"Genshin Impact\" and confirm to update.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePlease do not hesitate to contact Customer Service if you encounter any issues installing the new version. We will do our very best to resolve the issue.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e〓Update Details〓\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eI. New Areas\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNew Region Now Available: Snezhnaya\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ New Areas: Version 7.0 introduces the following new areas, \"Volkodlak Tundra,\" \"White Birch Snowgrave,\" \"Everfrozen Earth,\" \"Flamefeather Valley,\" and \"Fellfrost Peak\" in the Snezhnaya region.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e※ Completing Archon Quest Prologue: Act III \"Song of the Dragon and Freedom\" will automatically unlock a Teleport Waypoint southwest of the Volkodlak Tundra in Snezhnaya (If you have already completed this Archon Quest, the Teleport Waypoint will be unlocked after the update). You can use this Teleport Waypoint to head over to Snezhnaya. You'll also receive the Primogem reward for this Teleport Waypoint when it unlocks automatically.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e▌New System in Snezhnaya\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ \"Meeting Points\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eCryo Sigils obtained while adventuring in the frozen expanse of Snezhnaya can be used to construct the following Meeting Points with your companions at various locations after certain other conditions have also been met: \"Tidesong Cavern,\" \"Huntsman's Cabin,\" and \"The Korolevskiy Theater.\" Then, keep raising Meeting Point Levels to earn valuable supplies.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ \"Huntsman's Cabin\" Unlock Criteria:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Progress through \"Gunfire in the Silent Lands\" in the Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy\" to unlock.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ \"Tidesong Cavern\" \u0026amp; \"The Korolevskiy Theater\" Unlock Criteria:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Progress through \"Silence Alone is Disfavored\" in the Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy\" to unlock.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eExpeditions, Daily Commissions, and other new content will also be added in Snezhnaya.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ Snezhnaya Daily Commissions Unlock Criteria:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Progress through \"Great Deeds on the Tundra\" in the Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy\" to unlock.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAdds the Snezhnaya Fishing Association, where Travelers can exchange for new items here.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn addition, there will be new Fishing Points and \"Radiant Spincrystals\" in Snezhnaya.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eII. New Characters\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\"Swirling Snow\" Odette (Cryo) (5-Star)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ Stellar Linchpin: Cryo\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ Weapon: Sword\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ A famed ballerina of Snezhnaya, she blossoms against the frozen landscape with a beauty as sharp as frost.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Odette is a support character who enables the party to trigger Stellar-Conduct and Stellar Swirl reactions. She can continuously deal Stellar Glimmer DMG (Stellar-Conduct/Stellar Swirl) from off-field, provide consistent Cryo application, and increase the party's Stellar Glimmer DMG.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTraveler (Cryo) (5-Star)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ After resonating with Cryo, the Traveler enables the party to trigger Stellar Glimmer (Stellar-Conduct/Stellar Swirl). They can deal damage from off-field and in quick-swap rotations, and can also serve as an on-field DPS while in the \"Radiance: Stellar-Conduct\" state.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\"Swift-Striding Hound\" Alyosha (Electro) (4-Star)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ Vision: Electro\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ Weapon: Polearm\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ A \"professional hunter\" mastering the Snezhnayan snowfields. Beneath his calm demeanor, a fiercely distinct \"ideal\" seems to burn.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Alyosha is a support character who heals party members while continuously dealing Electro DMG.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIII. New Equipment\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. Event-Exclusive Weapon\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhitelake Frostfeather (5-Star Sword)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhitelake Frostfeather (Sword) greatly boosts ATK and Stellar Glimmer CRIT DMG, while also restoring Elemental Energy.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ The event-exclusive 5-star weapon Whitelake Frostfeather (Sword) can be obtained from the Event Wish. Please refer to the relevant official Event Notices for specific acquisition details.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e2. Special Weapon\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eExaiphanes Blade (5-Star Sword)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eExaiphanes Blade (Sword) greatly boosts the Traveler's ATK and restores Elemental Energy upon hitting an opponent.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Exaiphanes Blade (Sword) can be obtained by progressing through \"Great Deeds on the Tundra\" in Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ You can enhance your Exaiphanes Blade after using Cryo to awaken and connect to the Statues of The Seven in Snezhnaya.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e3. Forgeable Weapons\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNew Forgeable Weapons (4-Star)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEmberwell (Sword): Triggering an Elemental Reaction increases ATK, and triggering a Stellar Glimmer Reaction increases Stellar Glimmer DMG.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eBlade of Atonement (Claymore): Triggering an Elemental Reaction increases Elemental Mastery, and triggering a Stellar Glimmer Reaction increases ATK.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSong of the Vigil (Polearm): Triggering an Elemental Reaction restores Elemental Energy, and triggering a Stellar Glimmer Reaction increases ATK.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEchoes of the Heart (Catalyst): Triggering an Elemental Reaction increases Elemental Mastery, and triggering a Stellar Glimmer Reaction increases Stellar Glimmer DMG.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eCovenant of Frost and Snow (Bow): Increases Elemental Mastery when the equipping character uses an Elemental Skill.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ You can exchange for Weapon Forging Blueprints from Kuzmichev in Snezhnograd of Snezhnaya by consuming certain amounts and types of materials.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e4. Battle Pass Weapons\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNew Battle Pass Weapons (4-Star)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eHeretic's Molten Blade (Sword): Grants an ATK bonus after the equipping character uses an Elemental Skill. The bonus increases based on the distance they travel.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eForged by the Golden Melody (Claymore): Successively grants bonuses to ATK, Elemental Mastery, and Stellar Glimmer DMG.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFrostbreath (Polearm): grants an ATK bonus when the equipping character triggers a Cryo- or Hydro-related reaction, while also restoring Elemental Energy to party members.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eClash of Kings (Catalyst): Increases ATK and Elemental Mastery when the equipping character uses an Elemental Skill.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eJade Vista (Bow): Grants either an Elemental Mastery or ATK bonus depending on whether other party members share the equipping character's Elemental Type.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ 5 new weapons will be added to the BP Bounty. After unlocking the Gnostic Hymn and reaching Level 30, Travelers can select 1 weapon from a total of 15 as a reward.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e5. New Artifact Sets\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eScarlet Proof (4-Star and 5-Star)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ 2-Piece Set: ATK +18%.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ 4-Piece Set: Increases the equipping character's CRIT Rate by 16%, and their Stellar Swirl reaction dealt by 40%, for 10s after they trigger a Stellar Swirl reaction.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eHeart of the Furnace (4-Star and 5-Star)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ 2-Piece Set: ATK +18%.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ 4-Piece Set: Increases the equipping character's ATK by 12% for 12s when they trigger a Stellar Glimmer reaction or deal Stellar Glimmer reaction DMG. Also increases Stellar Glimmer reaction DMG dealt by all nearby party members by 50%. The above effects can trigger even when the equipping character is not on the field, and the DMG bonus from multiple Artifact Sets with the same name does not stack.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eHow to Obtain: Challenge the new Domain of Blessing in Everfrozen Earth, Snezhnaya, \"Inverted Glacier.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIV. New Main Story\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. New Archon Quest\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eChapter VII: Act I - Everwinter Without Mercy\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePermanently available after the Version 7.0 update\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Quest Unlock Criteria:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Adventure Rank 18 or above\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Complete the Archon Quest \"Prologue: Act III - Song of the Dragon and Freedom\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• The \"Focused Experience Mode\" function is available for this quest.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eChapter VII: Act II - Wraith's Nocturne\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePermanently available after the Version 7.0 update\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Quest Unlock Criteria:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Adventure Rank 18 or above\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Complete Chapter VII: Act I - \"Everwinter Without Mercy\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• The \"Focused Experience Mode\" function is available for this quest.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e※ Travelers who meet the unlock requirements can use the automatically unlocked Teleport Waypoint to reach Snezhnaya and begin Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy\" even if they have not completed the preceding Archon Quests, such as \"Song of the Welkin Moon: Act X.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e2. New World Quests\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNew World Quests\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\"Hesperides of Love and Hate\" Quest Chain, \"In the Dwelling of Life\" Quest Chain, \"On One Side a Palace, On the Other a Tomb\" Quest Chain, \"Her Palace Collapses Into the Blizzard\" Quest Chain, \"Mean Streets of the Despicable\" Quest Chain, \"The Soft Song She Sang\" Quest Chain, \"In the Tranquility of Cycles\" Quest Chain, \"Small Jack Frost, Big Problems,\" \"Forested Snowfield,\" \"For an Ice Mirror Fragment,\" and more.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e※ Progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy\" and complete \"Gunfire in the Silent Lands\" to unlock these quests.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eV. Elemental Reaction\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNew Stellar Glimmer Reaction: Stellar Swirl\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eUnder certain conditions, Anemo and Cryo can trigger Stellar Swirl, dealing one instance of Anemo DMG to the target and creating a Stellar Vortex. Only one Stellar Vortex can exist within the same area at a time.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eA Stellar Vortex detonates after a short delay, dealing AoE Cryo DMG. Triggering Stellar Swirl nearby a certain number of times increases the vortex's level, expanding its blast radius and increasing its DMG. Triggering additional Stellar Swirl reactions nearby can also cause the vortex to detonate early. The aforementioned DMG can trigger CRIT Hits.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen the Stellar Vortex explodes, it will also grant nearby characters the ability to jump higher once, for a short time.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, triggering Stellar Swirl grants certain nearby characters the \"Radiance: Stellar Swirl\" effect, enhancing some of their Talents and skill effects.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eCertain characters can also utilize their Talents to deal Stellar Swirl DMG to enemies. This DMG can trigger CRIT Hits.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eVI. New Enemies\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eImmortal Construct\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ A nigh-immortal life form created through bio-alchemy.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Immortal Construct burns its life to enter the \"Lifeflare\" state, in which it gains several HP shields at one time. Any DMG dealt by it while in this state will restore its HP. When the number of HP-restoring shields goes below a certain number or after Lifeflare lasts for a set time, the Immortal Construct will attempt to unleash \"Scorching Radiance.\" To stop it, you must break all of its HP shields.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Immortal Construct will be unable to recover any HP when affected by Stellar Glimmer reactions, no matter what it does...\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eLocated in Everfrozen Earth\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eChimeric Winged Lion\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ A product of bio-alchemy, and one of the flawed artificial monsters cast aside in pursuit of a certain grand ambition.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Chimeric Winged Lion will oscillate between two enhanced states: \"Thundercall\" and \"Galeforce.\" When it is in the Thundercall state, it will become weakened when its Elemental Ward is broken. Additionally, any attempts by it to spread its thunder blades can be disrupted by the Stellar Glimmer reaction. When it is in the Galeforce state, it will attempt to absorb any Anemo Orbs that are on the field to charge its attack. At this time, destroying the orbs or using the Stellar Glimmer reaction can stop its charging and weaken it.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eLocated in Volkodlak Tundra\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWildwood Leshy\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eRugged Elder Leshy, Juvenile Tree Segment\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ A species of Snezhnayan fae, these tree spirits inhabit the forests and wilds. Certain aspects of their behavior can be disrupted by the Stellar Glimmer Reaction.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eVolkodlak Brute\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eVoywolf Hunter, Fanged Zealot, Leomastiff Guard, Channel Contact, Long-Eared Striker, Volkodlak Raider, Volkodlak Sharpshooter, Volkodlak Basher, Volkodlak Lobber\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ A species of Snezhnayan fae, the Volkodlak comprise numerous distinct clans. Certain aspects of their behavior can be disrupted by the Stellar Glimmer Reaction.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAberrant Chimeric Monsters\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eChimeric Horned Bear, Chimeric Burrowbeast, Chimeric Armored Beast, Chimeric Winged Elephant\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ A product of bio-alchemy that was once widespread across the frozen lands, an aberrant chimeric monster. Certain aspects of their behavior can be disrupted by the Stellar Glimmer Reaction.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eOther Fae\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eGlacial Warden, Glaciomancer\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ A species of Snezhnayan fae, Snegoviks live for love amid the snow and ice. While in certain states, they become susceptible to disruption from the Stellar Glimmer Reaction.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinged Halberd-Knight, Winged Soarer Knight\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ A species of Snezhnayan fae, these winged Vila can fly. Certain aspects of their behavior can be disrupted by the Stellar Glimmer Reaction.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eVII. New Domains\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDomain of Forgery: Scars of Cursed Obsession\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ Challenge the Domain to obtain Weapon Ascension Materials.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ Unlock Criteria (satisfy any one of the criteria below to unlock):\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Reach Adventure Rank 10 or above\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Complete \"Knights of Favonius\" in Archon Quest Prologue: Act I \"The Outlander Who Caught the Wind\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDomain of Mastery: Relics of the Fallen Grace\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ Challenge the Domain to obtain Character Talent Materials.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ Unlock Criteria (satisfy any one of the criteria below to unlock):\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Reach Adventure Rank 10 or above\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Complete \"Knights of Favonius\" in Archon Quest Prologue: Act I \"The Outlander Who Caught the Wind\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDomain of Blessing: Inverted Glacier\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ Challenge the Domain to obtain artifacts in the \"Scarlet Proof\" and \"Heart of the Furnace\" sets.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ Unlock Criteria (satisfy any one of the criteria below to unlock):\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Reach Adventure Rank 10 or above\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Complete \"Knights of Favonius\" in Archon Quest Prologue: Act I \"The Outlander Who Caught the Wind\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eVIII. System Update\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. New Items\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEye of Graeae\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ A strange mechanism you encountered in an abandoned station in Snezhnaya. It often appears in the form of a monocle.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Eye of Graeae provides a variety of convenient functions. Travelers can use it to call a train and travel between cities, craft items or claim Daily Commission rewards while aboard, and create various Prime Ice Constructs to assist with exploration and adventuring.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Unlock Criteria\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Unlocks as you progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e2. New Gameplay\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThird-Person Shooter Combat Gameplay\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eUse a variety of firearms and equipment to defeat opponents through Elemental Reactions in the Shadow Realm.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs you progress through your adventure and unlock new gameplay, you will gain access to a variety of firearms and equipment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Unlock Criteria\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• This combat gameplay mode becomes available as you progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e▌ After unlocking the Third-Person Shooter Combat Gameplay, Travelers can take part in the associated \"Special Recruitment Project: Cycle Training\" to obtain rewards.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ Each week, you can accept new Training Quests from Yarovaya, in which you are tasked with entering and cleaning up specific Shadow Realms. Complete a certain number of these weekly quests to obtain various rewards.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Unlock Criteria\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act II \"Wraith's Nocturne\" to unlock the prerequisite quest. Complete that quest to gain access to this feature.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e▌ At the shooting range onboard the train, you can undertake special challenges at the simulated Shadow Realm \"Edge of Survival.\" This is where you can push your enemy-clearing skills to the limit and sharpen your proficiency with firearms.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eMore \"Edge of Survival\" stages will be added in future versions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEach \"Edge of Survival\" challenge stage has its own Frontrunners' Edge section with \"All Records\" and \"Friends' Records\" tabs, allowing Travelers to view the challenge results of other Travelers and their friends.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e*The \"All Records\" tab becomes available on August 17 once data compilation is complete.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePrime Ice Construct\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTravelers can use the Eye of Graeae to create a variety of Prime Ice Constructs throughout the open world.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePrime Ice Constructs can aid in exploration in the open world and allow Travelers to leave behind messages and materials to assist those in other worlds.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhile exploring Snezhnaya, Travelers may come across Prime Ice Constructs created by other Travelers. These constructs can help make exploration easier.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, Travelers can also give a Like to any Prime Ice Constructs they find helpful, while their own constructs may likewise receive Likes when they assist Travelers in other worlds.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Unlock Criteria\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy\" and complete \"Gunfire in the Silent Lands\" to unlock this feature.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e3. New System\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSnezhnaya Adventure Journal\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ The Snezhnaya Adventure Journal records your progress through adventures in Snezhnaya, along with content yet to be explored and rewards waiting to be claimed. You can use it as a one-stop overview of what remains to be explored in Snezhnaya and to track the relevant quests.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Unlock Criteria\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e• Progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy\" and complete \"Gunfire in the Silent Lands\" to unlock this feature.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e4. Gameplay Update\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eStellar-Conduct: \"Starlight Prism\" — Open-World Interaction Update\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn certain places in Snezhnaya, a Starlight Prism will also generate a Prism Mirage that lasts for a short time at the same location when it vanishes. Approach the mirage to activate the Starlight Prism again, at which point it will remain on the field permanently.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePrisms activated by such interactions have a chance to appear in other Travelers' worlds. Similarly, Prisms from other Travelers' worlds may also appear in your world.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWithin the Polestar Field created by a Starlight Prism, the Eye of Graeae's energy will not deplete and will remain at or above 30%. Prime Ice Constructs inside a Polestar Field will gain various wondrous buffs.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIX. Miliastra Wonderland\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eMiliastra Wonderland Update\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Cosmetic Sets\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe \"Phantasmagoric Discourse\" Event Ode brings 4 new sets: \"Whimsical Spectacle,\" \"Azure Mountainshade,\" \"Sleuth's Verdict,\" and \"Twilight Phantom Thief.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\"Chronicles of the Realms\"/\"Epic of the Realms\" features 3 new sets: \"Letter Crane Courier,\" \"Scary Cat,\" and \"Precision Strike.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAvailable for a limited time only from the Miliastra Shop: 3 new sets. They are \"Cloudbound Journey/Cloudbound Flight,\" \"Fun Under Open Skies,\" and \"Warrior of the Winning Hand.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\"Encounter Echoes\" Standard Ode: 1 new Set Catalog, \"Crowned by the Breeze,\" is available.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTake part in the \"Raiment Collection: Gentle Warmth\" event to obtain the new \"Amber Nectar\" set.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAfter the version update, the set \"Dreamy Summer Leisure\" that was obtainable through an earlier limited-time event will be available for a limited time at the Miliastra Shop.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Lobby\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWith the new version update, the Public Lobby will be changed to a new theme: \"Miracle Theater: Dreamcraft.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTravelers can purchase the new Private Lobby \"Miracle Theater: Light and Shadow Spectacle\" through the Miliastra Pass.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Wonderlands\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAdds the \"Wonderland Rising Stars\" section, which showcases the latest creations and updates from Craftspeople.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAdds the \"Wonderland Topic\" section, featuring regularly updated selections of Wonderland stages curated around specific themes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAdds replies to stage comments. Comments now show how long the commenter had played the stage when posting, as well as whether the stage was in Early Access at the time. The stage details page now displays the stage's recommendation rate over the past 30 days, calculated from comments posted during that period.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe new version also adds additional cosmetic components, expressions, and special effects.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor updates regarding the \"Miliastra Wonderland\" stage editor and Miliastra Sandbox, Travelers can check \"My Miliastra Wonderland\" \u0026gt; \"Notices.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eX. Genius Invokation TCG\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eGenius Invokation TCG Gameplay Update\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNew Character Card: Durin, Jahoda, and their corresponding Talent cards. Corresponding invitation duel and guest challenges have been added to the Player List.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNew Character Card: Hydro Hypostasis and the corresponding Talent card. The Tavern Challenge has also been added.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNew Action Cards \"Witch's Homework,\" \"Feasting in a Shared Toast,\" \"Temporal Wind's Eulogy,\" \"Phantasmal Nocturne,\" \"Genesis of Starsigns,\" and \"Sparkborne Magic\" have been added, which can be purchased from Prince at The Cat's Tail.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eNew Card Back \"Snezhnaya\" can be purchased from Prince at The Cat's Tail after reaching the corresponding Player Level.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Forge Realm's Temper is once again available. The theme of this edition is \"The Forge Realm's Temper: Game of Wits\":\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e(1) During The Forge Realm's Temper: Game of Wits, some stages will have special victory and defeat conditions or unique Special Rules. Adeptly adapt your tactics to complete the challenge and avoid the conditions for defeat!\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e(2) Within The Forge Realm's Temper: Game of Wits event stages, there will also be special victory or defeat rules that can easily exert influence on the tempo of the match. Fully utilizing these special rules will contribute greatly to your success.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eXI. Imaginarium Theater\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eUpdate Scheduled for September 1\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAfter the Version 7.0 update, a new season of Imaginarium Theater will be available on September 1, 2026.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eRequired Elemental Types: Hydro, Electro, and Dendro\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eOpening Characters: Columbina, Xingqiu, Cyno, Kuki Shinobu, Lauma, and Kaveh\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen Imaginarium Theater is open, the corresponding Opening Characters will obtain Fantastical Blessings.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSpecial Guest Stars: Odette, Sandrone, Sucrose, and Nicole\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAfter the new season of Imaginarium Theater begins, the characters Flins, Columbina, Kirara, and Illuga will each gain a new \"Thespian Trick\" that can be exchanged from the NPC Wolfy.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEnvisaged Echoes Update\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAfter the Version 7.0 update, new challenge stages and Echo cosmetics for Tartaglia and Xiao will be added.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eXII. Spiral Abyss\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eUpdate Scheduled for August 16\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ After the Version 7.0 update, Phase 1 of the Spiral Abyss will be updated on August 16.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Floor 9 Ley Line Disorder changed to:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eCharacters' Stellar Swirl DMG increased by 50%.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Floor 10 Ley Line Disorder changed to:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eCharacters' Stellar-Conduct DMG increased by 50%.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Floor 11 Ley Line Disorder changed to:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAll party members receive a 60% Cryo DMG Bonus.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAll party members gain a 60% Pyro DMG Bonus.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Floor 12 Ley Line Disorders changed to:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFirst Half: Characters' Superconduct DMG increased by 200% and Stellar-Conduct DMG increased by 75%.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSecond Half: Characters' Normal Attack Pyro DMG increased by 75%.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Updated the monster lineup on Floors 9, 10, 11, and 12 of the Spiral Abyss.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Blessing of the Abyssal Moon:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eLuster-Piercing Moon\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhile the active character is inside a Polestar Field, when they deal DMG to opponents, their attacks will unleash a shockwave at the opponent's position that deals True DMG. This can trigger once every 4s.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ Starting from this edition of Spiral Abyss, the \"Disenchantment in Deep Shadow\" and \"Celestial Gift\" Artifact set rewards in Domain Reliquary: Tier I and Domain Reliquary: Tier II obtained from the Ley Lines on Floors 9–12 will be replaced with the \"Scarlet Proof\" and the \"Heart of the Furnace\" sets.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eUpdate Scheduled for September 16\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◇ After the Version 7.0 update, Phase 2 of the Spiral Abyss will be updated on September 16.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Floor 11 Ley Line Disorder changed to:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAll party members gain a 60% Anemo DMG Bonus.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAll party members gain a 60% Electro DMG Bonus.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Floor 12 Ley Line Disorders changed to:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFirst Half: Characters' Swirl DMG increased by 200% and Stellar Swirl DMG increased by 75%.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSecond Half: Characters' Electro-Charged DMG increased by 200% and Lunar-Charged DMG increased by 75%.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Updated the monster lineup on Floors 11 – 12 of the Spiral Abyss.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Blessing of the Abyssal Moon:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eCascading Moon\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen a character deals Swirl or Stellar Swirl DMG to an opponent, a shockwave will be unleashed at the opponent's position, dealing True DMG. This effect can be triggered once every 4s.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eXIII. Other Update Details\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. New Recipe:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e○ Exploration or Quest Rewards: \"Glupov Rye Bread,\" \"Stroganina,\" \"Rimecurrant Ice Creams,\" \"Snowball Blooms Atop Snowfields,\" and \"Snowrealm Okroshkas.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e○ From Snezhnaya NPC Buturlina: \"Podvorye Smoked Sausage,\" \"Borscht,\" and \"Medovik.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e○ From Snezhnaya NPC Tolstaya: \"Zharkoye\" and \"Snezhnaya Shashliks.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e2. New Character Specialty Dishes:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e○ Alyosha's specialty: \"The Bullseye Roast\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e○ Odette's specialty: Lakeside Snow Swan\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e3. Adds the \"Snezhnaya: Sacred City of Ice and Pale Star (I),\" \"Land of Surging Shadows,\" \"Meetings in Outrealm: Series VII,\" and \"Mortal Travails: Series VII\" Achievement categories, as well as new Achievements to the \"Wonders of the World\" category.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e4. Adds Set 51 of \"Paimon's Paintings\" chat emojis.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e5. Adds some prompts for loading screens.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e6. New Namecards:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\"Odette: The Singular Swan\": Reward for reaching Friendship Lv. 10 with Odette\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\"Alyosha: Sit\": Reward for reaching Friendship Lv. 10 with Alyosha\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\"Achievement: Resplendence\": Reward for completing all achievements under \"Meetings in Outrealm: Series VII\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\"Snezhnaya: Long Night\": Reward for completing all achievements under \"Snezhnaya: Sacred City of Ice and Pale Star (I)\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\"Achievement: Treading Snow\": Reward for completing all achievements under \"Mortal Travails: Series VII\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\"Snezhnaya: Fleeting Glimpses\": Reward for completing all Special Recruitment Project: Cycle Training quests\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\"Achievement: Enigmatic Core\": Reward for completing all achievements under \"Land of Surging Shadows\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\"Travel Notes: Frostfarer\": Reward obtained via the BP system\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e7. Another 2 sets of Artifacts are available to exchange in the Mystic Offering system: Night of the Sky's Unveiling and Silken Moon's Serenade.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e8. Adds new Wildlife: Nochhornowl, Red-Bellied Plover, Fuzzbadger, Severelk, Polyarbear, Fluffahog, Morozhound, White Sumpter Beast, Ledobug, and Kristall Bug. You can use the Omni-Ubiquity Net to capture certain wildlife species found in Snezhnaya.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e9. Adds new Fish: Charcoal Snowfin, Cream Snowfin, Moonlight Snowfin, Ruby Starbloom Fish, Frostpetal Starbloom Fish, and Iridescent Starbloom Fish.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e10. Adds some of the Harvestable seeds from Snezhnaya to the Seed Dispensary.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e11. Adds Series II of \"Valiant Chronicles,\" featuring 3 new Local Legends and the corresponding challenges introduced in this version: Bandersnatch, Churin, and Furiosa. Complete the required number of challenges to obtain the \"First Snow\" avatar frame.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e12. The August 10, 2026 update to \"To Temper Thyself and Journey Far\" expands the selection of available Stella Fortuna, adding Stella Fortuna for the following characters: Lyney, Wriothesley, Navia, Xianyun, Chiori, Sigewinne, Clorinde, Emilie, and Yumemizuki Mizuki.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAfter the Version 7.0 update, \"Long-Term Encounter Points\" will be reset. Travelers, please take note.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e〓Adjustments \u0026amp; Optimizations〓\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e● Quests\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. Adds a teleportation function for quest objectives: Some quest objective locations now support teleportation. Select a supported objective on the \"Map\" screen and click the \"Go\" button to teleport to the quest objective or a nearby location. (This feature initially applies to certain quests in the Version 7.0 update. Future versions expand support to more new quests and further optimize the feature.)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e● Enemies\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. Optimizes how attempts are counted for the related \"Valiant Chronicles\" challenge objective to: \"Before the Prism Slime first gathers light and swells, make sure it attempts to absorb energy no more than 2 times,\" so that the count more accurately reflects the enemy's skill actions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e● Exploration\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. Adjusts how Multi-Layered Maps are displayed on the \"Map\" screen to prevent the layouts of unexplored areas from being revealed prematurely and affecting the gameplay experience: A Multi-Layered Map and its corresponding button now appear only after the Traveler has reached or unlocked the relevant area (before this adjustment, Multi-Layered Maps were always visible). If the corresponding area contains a tracked point, including a tracked Teleport Waypoint, the Multi-Layered Map and its button remain visible.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e2. Optimizes the display logic when the \"Luna Treasure Compass\" and \"Segment-Domain Treasure Compass\" mark clues: Increases the display priority of Oculus icons to prevent them from being obscured by other icons. (The \"Cryo Treasure Compass\" introduced in Version 7.0 also incorporates this optimization.)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e3. Increases the pin limit on the Map from 300 to 350.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e● Adventurer Handbook\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. Optimizes the sorting logic on the \"Domains\" page of the Adventurer Handbook: All Domains are now consistently sorted based on the version in which they were added and their unlock status, with unlocked Domains from more recent versions appearing higher in the list.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e● Inventory\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. Increases the combined Inventory capacity for Character Development Items, Food, Materials, Gadgets, Quest Items, and Precious Items from 2,300 to 2,600.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e2. Increases the maximum number of Artifacts that can be stored in the Inventory from 2,400 to 2,700.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e● Audio\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. Optimizes the sound effects in certain scenes, interfaces, and quests.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e2. Optimizes Chinese and Japanese voice-over lines in certain quests.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e● Other\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. Adds gyroscope support for certain Android devices that do not have a magnetometer but support a gyroscope.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e2. Adjusts the visual effects of \"Stellar-Conduct\" and \"Starlight Prism\" when Graphics Quality is set to \"Low\" or \"Lowest\" to reduce performance load.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e〓Bug Fixes〓\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e● Quests\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. Fixes an issue where, sometimes under certain circumstances, the character would be teleported to an incorrect location and end up falling in an endless loop during the objective \"Flee from the spinning turbine\" in the World Quest \"Visitors From the Stars.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e● Enemies\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. Fixes an issue where the visual effects for certain attacks performed by the enemy \"Ruin Hunter\" would display incorrectly.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e2. Fixes an issue where the camera would behave abnormally when Sandrone used her Elemental Skill while the enemy Millennial Pearl Seahorse's Xenomare Pearl was damaged.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e3. Fixes an issue where, under certain circumstances, the enemy \"Prism Slime\" became stuck underground when disengaging from combat, with no way to reset its state.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e4. Fixes an issue whereby there is a chance that the enemy \"Moosh-Tehir\" behaves abnormally when using skills.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e5. Fixes an issue whereby the enemy \"Precursor's Secret Source Matrix of Overseer Network\" is unaffected by characters' taunting skills.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e6. Fixes an issue whereby, under certain circumstances, there is a small chance that Detection Devices deployed by the enemy \"Precursor's Secret Source Matrix of Overseer Network\" disappear unexpectedly.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e● Characters\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. Fixes an issue where, when Sandrone's Charged Attack was canceled and she changed direction, some of Fagio's skill effects would also follow her new orientation in error.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e2. Fixes an issue whereby, under certain circumstances, there is a chance that the animation for the first hit of Sandrone's Normal Attack stutters abnormally when she performs consecutive Normal Attacks.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e3. Fixes an issue where, under certain circumstances, the Elemental RES reduction effect of Venti's Constellation 6 would sometimes not take effect.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e4. Fixes an issue whereby, after Citlali equips the outfit \"Whispers of Stars and Smoke,\" Citlalin's movement trajectory becomes abnormal when the Jump button is held to perform a leap.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e5. Fixes an issue whereby, following the Version Luna VIII update, there is a chance that the shield generated by Diona's Elemental Skill has an abnormal duration.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e6. Fixes an issue whereby there is a chance that the ribbon on Aether's outfit \"As Heaven and Earth Are Made Anew\" clips through his hair.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e7. Fixes an issue whereby there is a chance that the ribbons on Lumine's outfits \"As Heaven and Earth Are Made Anew\" and \"Rising Star\" clip through her character model.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e8. Fixes an issue whereby, on mobile devices, certain lighting effects are missing from Lohen's Elemental Burst animation.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e9. Fixes an issue whereby, in Co-Op Mode, when multiple Travelers are each using Yae Miko and have unlocked the Talent \"Edict of Cleansing,\" there is a chance that enhanced Sesshou Sakura lightning strikes fail to trigger the additional Electro DMG provided by the \"Radiance: Stellar-Conduct\" effect upon hitting enemies.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e10. Fixes an issue whereby, under certain circumstances, after Cyno unlocks the Additional Talent \"A Star With Which to Start the Journey,\" there is a chance that an abnormal number of Elemental Particles are generated when his Elemental Skill hits an enemy.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e11. Fixes an issue whereby abnormal visual effects remain in Illuga's hands after he uses his Elemental Skill by holding the Skill button.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e● Audio\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. Fixes an error in the Chinese voice-over for the dialogue option \"How do you like it here?\" when interacting with Sandrone in the Serenitea Pot.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e2. Fixes an error in a voice-over line in the Archon Quests \"As All Falls to Emptiness\" and \"Ancient Shadows Re-Emerge.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e3. Fixes an issue where, following the Version \"Luna VIII\" update, the Chinese voice-over for certain lines was missing from Yelan's Travelers' Tales.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e4. Restores certain related voice-over lines that were missing whenever Columbina performed the first hit of her Normal Attack.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e● Miliastra Wonderland\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. Fixes an issue whereby, when using a keyboard and mouse on PC, there is a chance that some key inputs fail to register if multiple keys are pressed simultaneously in Miliastra Wonderland stages.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e● Serenitea Pot\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. Fixes an issue where, under certain circumstances, characters would clip into the furnishing \"Ripples in Miniature.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e2. Fixes an issue where the model of the furnishing \"Keys of Ingenuity\" was inconsistent with its icon and the model displayed in the \"Sunny Summer Fontinalia\" event.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e● System\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. Fixes an issue whereby certain settings changes made while playing \"Repertoire of Myriad Melodies\" are not saved after logging back in.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e2. Fixes an issue whereby character facial shading displays abnormally on the \"Character\" screen.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e3. Fixes an issue where, under certain circumstances, the Element of the Traveler was displayed incorrectly in the \"Challenge Record\" screen during Stygian Onslaught gameplay.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e4. Fixes an issue on mobile devices where, after using a controller to navigate from the \"Settings\" to the \"Pre-Install\" screen, players were then unable to exit the corresponding screen.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e5. Fixes an issue in certain screens or scenes where switching to characters wearing their new outfits (specifically Citlali's \"Whispers of Stars and Smoke\" and Charlotte's \"Hurlock Variations\") might occasionally cause minor lags.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e6. Fixes an issue in the \"Equipment\" and Weapon \u0026gt; Enhance screens where the weapon \"Ballad of the Fjords\" would display with an incorrect height.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e● Other\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. Fixes an issue in Imaginarium Theater whereby, when the duration of certain stacks of the Brilliant Blessing \"Bloom: Core Condensation\" expires, there is a chance that all stacks are incorrectly cleared.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e2. Fixes text errors in certain quests, interfaces, dialogues and descriptions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e3. Fixes an issue whereby the gadget \"Sandrone's Portable Tea Table\" can be placed inside the Knights of Favonius Headquarters when it should not be.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e4. Fixes an issue whereby, under certain circumstances, when selecting \"Send Invitation\" while using the gadget \"Sandrone's Portable Tea Table,\" there is a chance that the \"Cancel Quest\" button is also activated.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e5. Fixes an issue where the gadget \"Sandrone's Portable Tea Table\" could be placed while clipping through terrain and locations.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e6. Fixes an issue whereby, on certain mobile devices or on PCs with Graphics Quality set to \"Low\" or \"Lowest,\" certain particle effects persist abnormally after Sandrone uses a Charged Attack.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e7. Fixes some text errors in certain languages and optimizes text. (Note: Related in-game functions have not changed. Travelers can view the changes in different languages by going to the Paimon Menu \u0026gt; Settings \u0026gt; Language and changing the Game Language.)\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Optimizes inconsistencies between certain voice-overs and the corresponding lines.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e◆ Optimizes certain English translations.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e〓Genius Invokation TCG Balance Adjustment〓\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eGenius Invokation TCG Balance Adjustment\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e1. Adjusts the number of Elemental Dice required and DMG dealt by the Elemental Skill of the Character Card \"Ifa\": The Elemental Dice cost is adjusted from 2 Anemo Dice to 3, and the DMG dealt is adjusted from 1 Anemo DMG to 2 Anemo DMG.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e2. Adjusts the Radiant Hues enhancement effect \"Radiant Hues: Swift Shadow\" for the Elemental Skill of the Character Card \"Wayward Hermetic Spiritspeaker.\" Its effect is adjusted to: \"When you play Radiant Hues: Grant a random highest-cost card in your Hand Cost Reduction equal to the number of stacks of this status.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e3. Adjusts the Elemental Skill effect of the Character Card \"Wayward Hermetic Spiritspeaker\": Effect changed to \"Deal 1 Cryo DMG, and place 1 Radiant Hues third from the top of your deck. If this is one of the first 4 times this skill is being used this game, then select 1 of 3 random Radiant Hues enhancement effects.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e4. Adjusts the effects of \"Tonatiuh,\" a card generated by the Adventure effect. When Adventure Experience reaches 2, its effect is adjusted to \"Draw 1 card.\" The DMG dealt by \"Tide-Turning Sacred Lord\" is adjusted to 3 Piercing DMG.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e5. Adjusts the effect of the Event Card \"In Every House a Stove\" when played in the first Round. Its effect is adjusted to: \"If your deck initially contains at least 4/2 different Talent Cards, draw 2/1 Talent Cards.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e*This is a work of fiction and is not related to any actual people, events, groups, or organizations.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\"PlayStation\", \"PS5\", \"DualSense\", \"DUALSHOCK\" are registered trademarks or trademarks of Sony Interactive Entertainment Inc.\u003c/p\u003e","cover":"","view_type":1,"created_at":1786489203,"images":[],"post_status":{"is_top":false,"is_good":false,"is_official":false,"is_vote":false,"is_quiz_vote":false,"is_demoted":false,"is_hot":false},"topic_ids":[],"view_status":1,"max_floor":331,"is_original":1,"republish_authorization":2,"reply_time":"2026-08-22 04:17:21","is_deleted":0,"is_interactive":false,"structured_content":"[{\"insert\":{\"image\":\"https://upload-os-bbs.hoyolab.com/upload/2026/08/11/0/bce0963941ee2f288f37d8153053d04c_6055301608089306545.jpeg\"},\"attributes\":{\"align\":\"img-center\",\"height\":390,\"width\":1080,\"size\":\"90042\"}},{\"insert\":\"\\nDear Traveler,\\nBelow are the details of the Version 7.0 update \\\"Everwinter Without Mercy\\\" and the update compensation.\\n\\n〓Compensation Details〓\\nMaintenance Compensation: Primogems ×300 (60 Primogems per hour the servers are down)\\nIssue Fix Compensation: Primogems ×300 (please refer to the relevant compensation mail for more details)\\n\\n〓Scope of Compensation〓\\nMaintenance Compensation: Travelers who have reached Adventure Rank 5 or above by 2026/08/12 06:00 (UTC+8).\\nCompensation must be claimed before the end of Version 7.0.\\n\\nIssue Fix Compensation: Travelers who have reached Adventure Rank 5 or above by 2026/08/12 06:00 (UTC+8).\\nPlease log in and claim your compensation before 2026/08/15 06:00 (UTC+8).\\n\\nOur developers will distribute compensation to Travelers via in-game mail within 5 hours after the update maintenance is finished. The mail will expire after 30 days, so don't forget to claim the attached compensation in time.\\n\\n〓Update Schedule〓\\nUpdate maintenance begins 2026/08/12 06:00 (UTC+8) and is estimated to take 5 hours.\\n\\n〓How to Update Game Client〓\\nPC: Close the game, open the Genshin Impact Launcher, and click Update.\\niOS: Open the App Store and tap Update.\\nAndroid: Open the game and follow the directions on-screen.\\nPlayStation®: Highlight \\\"Genshin Impact\\\" from the Home screen, press the OPTIONS button and select \\\"Check for Update.\\\"\\nXbox Series X|S: Open the system main menu, select \\\"My games \\u0026 apps,\\\" select the \\\"Manage\\\" tab, and on the \\\"Updates\\\" page, find \\\"Genshin Impact\\\" and confirm to update.\\n\\nPlease do not hesitate to contact Customer Service if you encounter any issues installing the new version. We will do our very best to resolve the issue.\\n\\n〓Update Details〓\\nI. New Areas\\nNew Region Now Available: Snezhnaya\\n◇ New Areas: Version 7.0 introduces the following new areas, \\\"Volkodlak Tundra,\\\" \\\"White Birch Snowgrave,\\\" \\\"Everfrozen Earth,\\\" \\\"Flamefeather Valley,\\\" and \\\"Fellfrost Peak\\\" in the Snezhnaya region.\\n\\n※ Completing Archon Quest Prologue: Act III \\\"Song of the Dragon and Freedom\\\" will automatically unlock a Teleport Waypoint southwest of the Volkodlak Tundra in Snezhnaya (If you have already completed this Archon Quest, the Teleport Waypoint will be unlocked after the update). You can use this Teleport Waypoint to head over to Snezhnaya. You'll also receive the Primogem reward for this Teleport Waypoint when it unlocks automatically.\\n\\n▌New System in Snezhnaya\\n◇ \\\"Meeting Points\\\"\\nCryo Sigils obtained while adventuring in the frozen expanse of Snezhnaya can be used to construct the following Meeting Points with your companions at various locations after certain other conditions have also been met: \\\"Tidesong Cavern,\\\" \\\"Huntsman's Cabin,\\\" and \\\"The Korolevskiy Theater.\\\" Then, keep raising Meeting Point Levels to earn valuable supplies.\\n\\n◆ \\\"Huntsman's Cabin\\\" Unlock Criteria:\\n• Progress through \\\"Gunfire in the Silent Lands\\\" in the Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \\\"Everwinter Without Mercy\\\" to unlock.\\n◆ \\\"Tidesong Cavern\\\" \\u0026 \\\"The Korolevskiy Theater\\\" Unlock Criteria:\\n• Progress through \\\"Silence Alone is Disfavored\\\" in the Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \\\"Everwinter Without Mercy\\\" to unlock.\\n\\nExpeditions, Daily Commissions, and other new content will also be added in Snezhnaya.\\n◇ Snezhnaya Daily Commissions Unlock Criteria:\\n• Progress through \\\"Great Deeds on the Tundra\\\" in the Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \\\"Everwinter Without Mercy\\\" to unlock.\\n\\nAdds the Snezhnaya Fishing Association, where Travelers can exchange for new items here.\\nIn addition, there will be new Fishing Points and \\\"Radiant Spincrystals\\\" in Snezhnaya.\\n\\nII. New Characters\\n\\\"Swirling Snow\\\" Odette (Cryo) (5-Star)\\n◇ Stellar Linchpin: Cryo\\n◇ Weapon: Sword\\n◇ A famed ballerina of Snezhnaya, she blossoms against the frozen landscape with a beauty as sharp as frost.\\n\\n◆ Odette is a support character who enables the party to trigger Stellar-Conduct and Stellar Swirl reactions. She can continuously deal Stellar Glimmer DMG (Stellar-Conduct/Stellar Swirl) from off-field, provide consistent Cryo application, and increase the party's Stellar Glimmer DMG.\\n\\nTraveler (Cryo) (5-Star)\\n◆ After resonating with Cryo, the Traveler enables the party to trigger Stellar Glimmer (Stellar-Conduct/Stellar Swirl). They can deal damage from off-field and in quick-swap rotations, and can also serve as an on-field DPS while in the \\\"Radiance: Stellar-Conduct\\\" state.\\n\\n\\\"Swift-Striding Hound\\\" Alyosha (Electro) (4-Star)\\n◇ Vision: Electro\\n◇ Weapon: Polearm\\n◇ A \\\"professional hunter\\\" mastering the Snezhnayan snowfields. Beneath his calm demeanor, a fiercely distinct \\\"ideal\\\" seems to burn.\\n\\n◆ Alyosha is a support character who heals party members while continuously dealing Electro DMG.\\n\\nIII. New Equipment\\n1. Event-Exclusive Weapon\\nWhitelake Frostfeather (5-Star Sword)\\nWhitelake Frostfeather (Sword) greatly boosts ATK and Stellar Glimmer CRIT DMG, while also restoring Elemental Energy.\\n◆ The event-exclusive 5-star weapon Whitelake Frostfeather (Sword) can be obtained from the Event Wish. Please refer to the relevant official Event Notices for specific acquisition details.\\n\\n2. Special Weapon\\nExaiphanes Blade (5-Star Sword)\\nExaiphanes Blade (Sword) greatly boosts the Traveler's ATK and restores Elemental Energy upon hitting an opponent.\\n◆ Exaiphanes Blade (Sword) can be obtained by progressing through \\\"Great Deeds on the Tundra\\\" in Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \\\"Everwinter Without Mercy.\\\"\\n◆ You can enhance your Exaiphanes Blade after using Cryo to awaken and connect to the Statues of The Seven in Snezhnaya.\\n\\n3. Forgeable Weapons\\nNew Forgeable Weapons (4-Star)\\nEmberwell (Sword): Triggering an Elemental Reaction increases ATK, and triggering a Stellar Glimmer Reaction increases Stellar Glimmer DMG.\\nBlade of Atonement (Claymore): Triggering an Elemental Reaction increases Elemental Mastery, and triggering a Stellar Glimmer Reaction increases ATK.\\nSong of the Vigil (Polearm): Triggering an Elemental Reaction restores Elemental Energy, and triggering a Stellar Glimmer Reaction increases ATK.\\nEchoes of the Heart (Catalyst): Triggering an Elemental Reaction increases Elemental Mastery, and triggering a Stellar Glimmer Reaction increases Stellar Glimmer DMG.\\nCovenant of Frost and Snow (Bow): Increases Elemental Mastery when the equipping character uses an Elemental Skill.\\n\\n◆ You can exchange for Weapon Forging Blueprints from Kuzmichev in Snezhnograd of Snezhnaya by consuming certain amounts and types of materials.\\n\\n4. Battle Pass Weapons\\nNew Battle Pass Weapons (4-Star)\\nHeretic's Molten Blade (Sword): Grants an ATK bonus after the equipping character uses an Elemental Skill. The bonus increases based on the distance they travel.\\nForged by the Golden Melody (Claymore): Successively grants bonuses to ATK, Elemental Mastery, and Stellar Glimmer DMG.\\nFrostbreath (Polearm): grants an ATK bonus when the equipping character triggers a Cryo- or Hydro-related reaction, while also restoring Elemental Energy to party members.\\nClash of Kings (Catalyst): Increases ATK and Elemental Mastery when the equipping character uses an Elemental Skill.\\nJade Vista (Bow): Grants either an Elemental Mastery or ATK bonus depending on whether other party members share the equipping character's Elemental Type.\\n\\n◆ 5 new weapons will be added to the BP Bounty. After unlocking the Gnostic Hymn and reaching Level 30, Travelers can select 1 weapon from a total of 15 as a reward.\\n\\n5. New Artifact Sets\\nScarlet Proof (4-Star and 5-Star)\\n◇ 2-Piece Set: ATK +18%.\\n◇ 4-Piece Set: Increases the equipping character's CRIT Rate by 16%, and their Stellar Swirl reaction dealt by 40%, for 10s after they trigger a Stellar Swirl reaction.\\n\\nHeart of the Furnace (4-Star and 5-Star)\\n◇ 2-Piece Set: ATK +18%.\\n◇ 4-Piece Set: Increases the equipping character's ATK by 12% for 12s when they trigger a Stellar Glimmer reaction or deal Stellar Glimmer reaction DMG. Also increases Stellar Glimmer reaction DMG dealt by all nearby party members by 50%. The above effects can trigger even when the equipping character is not on the field, and the DMG bonus from multiple Artifact Sets with the same name does not stack.\\nHow to Obtain: Challenge the new Domain of Blessing in Everfrozen Earth, Snezhnaya, \\\"Inverted Glacier.\\\"\\n\\nIV. New Main Story\\n1. New Archon Quest\\nChapter VII: Act I - Everwinter Without Mercy\\nPermanently available after the Version 7.0 update\\n\\n◆ Quest Unlock Criteria:\\n• Adventure Rank 18 or above\\n• Complete the Archon Quest \\\"Prologue: Act III - Song of the Dragon and Freedom\\\"\\n• The \\\"Focused Experience Mode\\\" function is available for this quest.\\n\\nChapter VII: Act II - Wraith's Nocturne\\nPermanently available after the Version 7.0 update\\n\\n◆ Quest Unlock Criteria:\\n• Adventure Rank 18 or above\\n• Complete Chapter VII: Act I - \\\"Everwinter Without Mercy\\\"\\n• The \\\"Focused Experience Mode\\\" function is available for this quest.\\n\\n※ Travelers who meet the unlock requirements can use the automatically unlocked Teleport Waypoint to reach Snezhnaya and begin Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \\\"Everwinter Without Mercy\\\" even if they have not completed the preceding Archon Quests, such as \\\"Song of the Welkin Moon: Act X.\\\"\\n\\n2. New World Quests\\nNew World Quests\\n\\\"Hesperides of Love and Hate\\\" Quest Chain, \\\"In the Dwelling of Life\\\" Quest Chain, \\\"On One Side a Palace, On the Other a Tomb\\\" Quest Chain, \\\"Her Palace Collapses Into the Blizzard\\\" Quest Chain, \\\"Mean Streets of the Despicable\\\" Quest Chain, \\\"The Soft Song She Sang\\\" Quest Chain, \\\"In the Tranquility of Cycles\\\" Quest Chain, \\\"Small Jack Frost, Big Problems,\\\" \\\"Forested Snowfield,\\\" \\\"For an Ice Mirror Fragment,\\\" and more.\\n※ Progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \\\"Everwinter Without Mercy\\\" and complete \\\"Gunfire in the Silent Lands\\\" to unlock these quests.\\n\\nV. Elemental Reaction\\nNew Stellar Glimmer Reaction: Stellar Swirl\\nUnder certain conditions, Anemo and Cryo can trigger Stellar Swirl, dealing one instance of Anemo DMG to the target and creating a Stellar Vortex. Only one Stellar Vortex can exist within the same area at a time.\\nA Stellar Vortex detonates after a short delay, dealing AoE Cryo DMG. Triggering Stellar Swirl nearby a certain number of times increases the vortex's level, expanding its blast radius and increasing its DMG. Triggering additional Stellar Swirl reactions nearby can also cause the vortex to detonate early. The aforementioned DMG can trigger CRIT Hits.\\nWhen the Stellar Vortex explodes, it will also grant nearby characters the ability to jump higher once, for a short time.\\n\\nAdditionally, triggering Stellar Swirl grants certain nearby characters the \\\"Radiance: Stellar Swirl\\\" effect, enhancing some of their Talents and skill effects.\\nCertain characters can also utilize their Talents to deal Stellar Swirl DMG to enemies. This DMG can trigger CRIT Hits.\\n\\nVI. New Enemies\\nImmortal Construct\\n◇ A nigh-immortal life form created through bio-alchemy.\\nThe Immortal Construct burns its life to enter the \\\"Lifeflare\\\" state, in which it gains several HP shields at one time. Any DMG dealt by it while in this state will restore its HP. When the number of HP-restoring shields goes below a certain number or after Lifeflare lasts for a set time, the Immortal Construct will attempt to unleash \\\"Scorching Radiance.\\\" To stop it, you must break all of its HP shields.\\nThe Immortal Construct will be unable to recover any HP when affected by Stellar Glimmer reactions, no matter what it does...\\nLocated in Everfrozen Earth\\n\\nChimeric Winged Lion\\n◇ A product of bio-alchemy, and one of the flawed artificial monsters cast aside in pursuit of a certain grand ambition.\\nThe Chimeric Winged Lion will oscillate between two enhanced states: \\\"Thundercall\\\" and \\\"Galeforce.\\\" When it is in the Thundercall state, it will become weakened when its Elemental Ward is broken. Additionally, any attempts by it to spread its thunder blades can be disrupted by the Stellar Glimmer reaction. When it is in the Galeforce state, it will attempt to absorb any Anemo Orbs that are on the field to charge its attack. At this time, destroying the orbs or using the Stellar Glimmer reaction can stop its charging and weaken it.\\nLocated in Volkodlak Tundra\\n\\nWildwood Leshy\\nRugged Elder Leshy, Juvenile Tree Segment\\n◇ A species of Snezhnayan fae, these tree spirits inhabit the forests and wilds. Certain aspects of their behavior can be disrupted by the Stellar Glimmer Reaction.\\n\\nVolkodlak Brute\\nVoywolf Hunter, Fanged Zealot, Leomastiff Guard, Channel Contact, Long-Eared Striker, Volkodlak Raider, Volkodlak Sharpshooter, Volkodlak Basher, Volkodlak Lobber\\n◇ A species of Snezhnayan fae, the Volkodlak comprise numerous distinct clans. Certain aspects of their behavior can be disrupted by the Stellar Glimmer Reaction.\\n\\nAberrant Chimeric Monsters\\nChimeric Horned Bear, Chimeric Burrowbeast, Chimeric Armored Beast, Chimeric Winged Elephant\\n◇ A product of bio-alchemy that was once widespread across the frozen lands, an aberrant chimeric monster. Certain aspects of their behavior can be disrupted by the Stellar Glimmer Reaction.\\n\\nOther Fae\\nGlacial Warden, Glaciomancer\\n◇ A species of Snezhnayan fae, Snegoviks live for love amid the snow and ice. While in certain states, they become susceptible to disruption from the Stellar Glimmer Reaction.\\n\\nWinged Halberd-Knight, Winged Soarer Knight\\n◇ A species of Snezhnayan fae, these winged Vila can fly. Certain aspects of their behavior can be disrupted by the Stellar Glimmer Reaction.\\n\\nVII. New Domains\\nDomain of Forgery: Scars of Cursed Obsession\\n◇ Challenge the Domain to obtain Weapon Ascension Materials.\\n◇ Unlock Criteria (satisfy any one of the criteria below to unlock):\\n• Reach Adventure Rank 10 or above\\n• Complete \\\"Knights of Favonius\\\" in Archon Quest Prologue: Act I \\\"The Outlander Who Caught the Wind\\\"\\n\\nDomain of Mastery: Relics of the Fallen Grace\\n◇ Challenge the Domain to obtain Character Talent Materials.\\n◇ Unlock Criteria (satisfy any one of the criteria below to unlock):\\n• Reach Adventure Rank 10 or above\\n• Complete \\\"Knights of Favonius\\\" in Archon Quest Prologue: Act I \\\"The Outlander Who Caught the Wind\\\"\\nDomain of Blessing: Inverted Glacier\\n◇ Challenge the Domain to obtain artifacts in the \\\"Scarlet Proof\\\" and \\\"Heart of the Furnace\\\" sets.\\n◇ Unlock Criteria (satisfy any one of the criteria below to unlock):\\n• Reach Adventure Rank 10 or above\\n• Complete \\\"Knights of Favonius\\\" in Archon Quest Prologue: Act I \\\"The Outlander Who Caught the Wind\\\"\\n\\nVIII. System Update\\n1. New Items\\nEye of Graeae\\n◇ A strange mechanism you encountered in an abandoned station in Snezhnaya. It often appears in the form of a monocle.\\nThe Eye of Graeae provides a variety of convenient functions. Travelers can use it to call a train and travel between cities, craft items or claim Daily Commission rewards while aboard, and create various Prime Ice Constructs to assist with exploration and adventuring.\\n\\n◆ Unlock Criteria\\n• Unlocks as you progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \\\"Everwinter Without Mercy.\\\"\\n\\n2. New Gameplay\\nThird-Person Shooter Combat Gameplay\\nUse a variety of firearms and equipment to defeat opponents through Elemental Reactions in the Shadow Realm.\\nAs you progress through your adventure and unlock new gameplay, you will gain access to a variety of firearms and equipment.\\n\\n◆ Unlock Criteria\\n• This combat gameplay mode becomes available as you progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \\\"Everwinter Without Mercy.\\\"\\n\\n▌ After unlocking the Third-Person Shooter Combat Gameplay, Travelers can take part in the associated \\\"Special Recruitment Project: Cycle Training\\\" to obtain rewards.\\n◇ Each week, you can accept new Training Quests from Yarovaya, in which you are tasked with entering and cleaning up specific Shadow Realms. Complete a certain number of these weekly quests to obtain various rewards.\\n\\n◆ Unlock Criteria\\n• Progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act II \\\"Wraith's Nocturne\\\" to unlock the prerequisite quest. Complete that quest to gain access to this feature.\\n\\n▌ At the shooting range onboard the train, you can undertake special challenges at the simulated Shadow Realm \\\"Edge of Survival.\\\" This is where you can push your enemy-clearing skills to the limit and sharpen your proficiency with firearms.\\nMore \\\"Edge of Survival\\\" stages will be added in future versions.\\nEach \\\"Edge of Survival\\\" challenge stage has its own Frontrunners' Edge section with \\\"All Records\\\" and \\\"Friends' Records\\\" tabs, allowing Travelers to view the challenge results of other Travelers and their friends.\\n*The \\\"All Records\\\" tab becomes available on August 17 once data compilation is complete.\\n\\nPrime Ice Construct\\nTravelers can use the Eye of Graeae to create a variety of Prime Ice Constructs throughout the open world.\\nPrime Ice Constructs can aid in exploration in the open world and allow Travelers to leave behind messages and materials to assist those in other worlds.\\nWhile exploring Snezhnaya, Travelers may come across Prime Ice Constructs created by other Travelers. These constructs can help make exploration easier.\\nAdditionally, Travelers can also give a Like to any Prime Ice Constructs they find helpful, while their own constructs may likewise receive Likes when they assist Travelers in other worlds.\\n\\n◆ Unlock Criteria\\n• Progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \\\"Everwinter Without Mercy\\\" and complete \\\"Gunfire in the Silent Lands\\\" to unlock this feature.\\n\\n3. New System\\nSnezhnaya Adventure Journal\\n◇ The Snezhnaya Adventure Journal records your progress through adventures in Snezhnaya, along with content yet to be explored and rewards waiting to be claimed. You can use it as a one-stop overview of what remains to be explored in Snezhnaya and to track the relevant quests.\\n◆ Unlock Criteria\\n• Progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \\\"Everwinter Without Mercy\\\" and complete \\\"Gunfire in the Silent Lands\\\" to unlock this feature.\\n\\n4. Gameplay Update\\nStellar-Conduct: \\\"Starlight Prism\\\" — Open-World Interaction Update\\nIn certain places in Snezhnaya, a Starlight Prism will also generate a Prism Mirage that lasts for a short time at the same location when it vanishes. Approach the mirage to activate the Starlight Prism again, at which point it will remain on the field permanently.\\nPrisms activated by such interactions have a chance to appear in other Travelers' worlds. Similarly, Prisms from other Travelers' worlds may also appear in your world.\\nWithin the Polestar Field created by a Starlight Prism, the Eye of Graeae's energy will not deplete and will remain at or above 30%. Prime Ice Constructs inside a Polestar Field will gain various wondrous buffs.\\n\\nIX. Miliastra Wonderland\\nMiliastra Wonderland Update\\n◆ Cosmetic Sets\\nThe \\\"Phantasmagoric Discourse\\\" Event Ode brings 4 new sets: \\\"Whimsical Spectacle,\\\" \\\"Azure Mountainshade,\\\" \\\"Sleuth's Verdict,\\\" and \\\"Twilight Phantom Thief.\\\"\\n\\\"Chronicles of the Realms\\\"/\\\"Epic of the Realms\\\" features 3 new sets: \\\"Letter Crane Courier,\\\" \\\"Scary Cat,\\\" and \\\"Precision Strike.\\\"\\nAvailable for a limited time only from the Miliastra Shop: 3 new sets. They are \\\"Cloudbound Journey/Cloudbound Flight,\\\" \\\"Fun Under Open Skies,\\\" and \\\"Warrior of the Winning Hand.\\\"\\n\\\"Encounter Echoes\\\" Standard Ode: 1 new Set Catalog, \\\"Crowned by the Breeze,\\\" is available.\\nTake part in the \\\"Raiment Collection: Gentle Warmth\\\" event to obtain the new \\\"Amber Nectar\\\" set.\\nAfter the version update, the set \\\"Dreamy Summer Leisure\\\" that was obtainable through an earlier limited-time event will be available for a limited time at the Miliastra Shop.\\n\\n◆ Lobby\\nWith the new version update, the Public Lobby will be changed to a new theme: \\\"Miracle Theater: Dreamcraft.\\\"\\nTravelers can purchase the new Private Lobby \\\"Miracle Theater: Light and Shadow Spectacle\\\" through the Miliastra Pass.\\n\\n◆ Wonderlands\\nAdds the \\\"Wonderland Rising Stars\\\" section, which showcases the latest creations and updates from Craftspeople.\\nAdds the \\\"Wonderland Topic\\\" section, featuring regularly updated selections of Wonderland stages curated around specific themes.\\nAdds replies to stage comments. Comments now show how long the commenter had played the stage when posting, as well as whether the stage was in Early Access at the time. The stage details page now displays the stage's recommendation rate over the past 30 days, calculated from comments posted during that period.\\n\\nThe new version also adds additional cosmetic components, expressions, and special effects.\\n\\nFor updates regarding the \\\"Miliastra Wonderland\\\" stage editor and Miliastra Sandbox, Travelers can check \\\"My Miliastra Wonderland\\\" \\u003e \\\"Notices.\\\"\\n\\nX. Genius Invokation TCG\\nGenius Invokation TCG Gameplay Update\\nNew Character Card: Durin, Jahoda, and their corresponding Talent cards. Corresponding invitation duel and guest challenges have been added to the Player List.\\nNew Character Card: Hydro Hypostasis and the corresponding Talent card. The Tavern Challenge has also been added.\\nNew Action Cards \\\"Witch's Homework,\\\" \\\"Feasting in a Shared Toast,\\\" \\\"Temporal Wind's Eulogy,\\\" \\\"Phantasmal Nocturne,\\\" \\\"Genesis of Starsigns,\\\" and \\\"Sparkborne Magic\\\" have been added, which can be purchased from Prince at The Cat's Tail.\\nNew Card Back \\\"Snezhnaya\\\" can be purchased from Prince at The Cat's Tail after reaching the corresponding Player Level.\\nThe Forge Realm's Temper is once again available. The theme of this edition is \\\"The Forge Realm's Temper: Game of Wits\\\":\\n(1) During The Forge Realm's Temper: Game of Wits, some stages will have special victory and defeat conditions or unique Special Rules. Adeptly adapt your tactics to complete the challenge and avoid the conditions for defeat!\\n(2) Within The Forge Realm's Temper: Game of Wits event stages, there will also be special victory or defeat rules that can easily exert influence on the tempo of the match. Fully utilizing these special rules will contribute greatly to your success.\\n\\nXI. Imaginarium Theater\\nUpdate Scheduled for September 1\\nAfter the Version 7.0 update, a new season of Imaginarium Theater will be available on September 1, 2026.\\n\\nRequired Elemental Types: Hydro, Electro, and Dendro\\nOpening Characters: Columbina, Xingqiu, Cyno, Kuki Shinobu, Lauma, and Kaveh\\nWhen Imaginarium Theater is open, the corresponding Opening Characters will obtain Fantastical Blessings.\\nSpecial Guest Stars: Odette, Sandrone, Sucrose, and Nicole\\nAfter the new season of Imaginarium Theater begins, the characters Flins, Columbina, Kirara, and Illuga will each gain a new \\\"Thespian Trick\\\" that can be exchanged from the NPC Wolfy.\\n\\nEnvisaged Echoes Update\\nAfter the Version 7.0 update, new challenge stages and Echo cosmetics for Tartaglia and Xiao will be added.\\n\\nXII. Spiral Abyss\\nUpdate Scheduled for August 16\\n◇ After the Version 7.0 update, Phase 1 of the Spiral Abyss will be updated on August 16.\\n\\n◆ Floor 9 Ley Line Disorder changed to:\\nCharacters' Stellar Swirl DMG increased by 50%.\\n\\n◆ Floor 10 Ley Line Disorder changed to:\\nCharacters' Stellar-Conduct DMG increased by 50%.\\n\\n◆ Floor 11 Ley Line Disorder changed to:\\nAll party members receive a 60% Cryo DMG Bonus.\\nAll party members gain a 60% Pyro DMG Bonus.\\n\\n◆ Floor 12 Ley Line Disorders changed to:\\nFirst Half: Characters' Superconduct DMG increased by 200% and Stellar-Conduct DMG increased by 75%.\\nSecond Half: Characters' Normal Attack Pyro DMG increased by 75%.\\n\\n◆ Updated the monster lineup on Floors 9, 10, 11, and 12 of the Spiral Abyss.\\n\\n◆ Blessing of the Abyssal Moon:\\nLuster-Piercing Moon\\nWhile the active character is inside a Polestar Field, when they deal DMG to opponents, their attacks will unleash a shockwave at the opponent's position that deals True DMG. This can trigger once every 4s.\\n\\n◇ Starting from this edition of Spiral Abyss, the \\\"Disenchantment in Deep Shadow\\\" and \\\"Celestial Gift\\\" Artifact set rewards in Domain Reliquary: Tier I and Domain Reliquary: Tier II obtained from the Ley Lines on Floors 9–12 will be replaced with the \\\"Scarlet Proof\\\" and the \\\"Heart of the Furnace\\\" sets.\\n\\nUpdate Scheduled for September 16\\n◇ After the Version 7.0 update, Phase 2 of the Spiral Abyss will be updated on September 16.\\n\\n◆ Floor 11 Ley Line Disorder changed to:\\nAll party members gain a 60% Anemo DMG Bonus.\\nAll party members gain a 60% Electro DMG Bonus.\\n\\n◆ Floor 12 Ley Line Disorders changed to:\\nFirst Half: Characters' Swirl DMG increased by 200% and Stellar Swirl DMG increased by 75%.\\nSecond Half: Characters' Electro-Charged DMG increased by 200% and Lunar-Charged DMG increased by 75%.\\n\\n◆ Updated the monster lineup on Floors 11 – 12 of the Spiral Abyss.\\n\\n◆ Blessing of the Abyssal Moon:\\nCascading Moon\\nWhen a character deals Swirl or Stellar Swirl DMG to an opponent, a shockwave will be unleashed at the opponent's position, dealing True DMG. This effect can be triggered once every 4s.\\n\\nXIII. Other Update Details\\n1. New Recipe:\\n○ Exploration or Quest Rewards: \\\"Glupov Rye Bread,\\\" \\\"Stroganina,\\\" \\\"Rimecurrant Ice Creams,\\\" \\\"Snowball Blooms Atop Snowfields,\\\" and \\\"Snowrealm Okroshkas.\\\"\\n○ From Snezhnaya NPC Buturlina: \\\"Podvorye Smoked Sausage,\\\" \\\"Borscht,\\\" and \\\"Medovik.\\\"\\n○ From Snezhnaya NPC Tolstaya: \\\"Zharkoye\\\" and \\\"Snezhnaya Shashliks.\\\"\\n2. New Character Specialty Dishes:\\n○ Alyosha's specialty: \\\"The Bullseye Roast\\\"\\n○ Odette's specialty: Lakeside Snow Swan\\n3. Adds the \\\"Snezhnaya: Sacred City of Ice and Pale Star (I),\\\" \\\"Land of Surging Shadows,\\\" \\\"Meetings in Outrealm: Series VII,\\\" and \\\"Mortal Travails: Series VII\\\" Achievement categories, as well as new Achievements to the \\\"Wonders of the World\\\" category.\\n4. Adds Set 51 of \\\"Paimon's Paintings\\\" chat emojis.\\n5. Adds some prompts for loading screens.\\n6. New Namecards:\\n\\\"Odette: The Singular Swan\\\": Reward for reaching Friendship Lv. 10 with Odette\\n\\\"Alyosha: Sit\\\": Reward for reaching Friendship Lv. 10 with Alyosha\\n\\\"Achievement: Resplendence\\\": Reward for completing all achievements under \\\"Meetings in Outrealm: Series VII\\\"\\n\\\"Snezhnaya: Long Night\\\": Reward for completing all achievements under \\\"Snezhnaya: Sacred City of Ice and Pale Star (I)\\\"\\n\\\"Achievement: Treading Snow\\\": Reward for completing all achievements under \\\"Mortal Travails: Series VII\\\"\\n\\\"Snezhnaya: Fleeting Glimpses\\\": Reward for completing all Special Recruitment Project: Cycle Training quests\\n\\\"Achievement: Enigmatic Core\\\": Reward for completing all achievements under \\\"Land of Surging Shadows\\\"\\n\\\"Travel Notes: Frostfarer\\\": Reward obtained via the BP system\\n7. Another 2 sets of Artifacts are available to exchange in the Mystic Offering system: Night of the Sky's Unveiling and Silken Moon's Serenade.\\n8. Adds new Wildlife: Nochhornowl, Red-Bellied Plover, Fuzzbadger, Severelk, Polyarbear, Fluffahog, Morozhound, White Sumpter Beast, Ledobug, and Kristall Bug. You can use the Omni-Ubiquity Net to capture certain wildlife species found in Snezhnaya.\\n9. Adds new Fish: Charcoal Snowfin, Cream Snowfin, Moonlight Snowfin, Ruby Starbloom Fish, Frostpetal Starbloom Fish, and Iridescent Starbloom Fish.\\n10. Adds some of the Harvestable seeds from Snezhnaya to the Seed Dispensary.\\n11. Adds Series II of \\\"Valiant Chronicles,\\\" featuring 3 new Local Legends and the corresponding challenges introduced in this version: Bandersnatch, Churin, and Furiosa. Complete the required number of challenges to obtain the \\\"First Snow\\\" avatar frame.\\n12. The August 10, 2026 update to \\\"To Temper Thyself and Journey Far\\\" expands the selection of available Stella Fortuna, adding Stella Fortuna for the following characters: Lyney, Wriothesley, Navia, Xianyun, Chiori, Sigewinne, Clorinde, Emilie, and Yumemizuki Mizuki.\\n\\nAfter the Version 7.0 update, \\\"Long-Term Encounter Points\\\" will be reset. Travelers, please take note.\\n\\n〓Adjustments \\u0026 Optimizations〓\\n● Quests\\n1. Adds a teleportation function for quest objectives: Some quest objective locations now support teleportation. Select a supported objective on the \\\"Map\\\" screen and click the \\\"Go\\\" button to teleport to the quest objective or a nearby location. (This feature initially applies to certain quests in the Version 7.0 update. Future versions expand support to more new quests and further optimize the feature.)\\n● Enemies\\n1. Optimizes how attempts are counted for the related \\\"Valiant Chronicles\\\" challenge objective to: \\\"Before the Prism Slime first gathers light and swells, make sure it attempts to absorb energy no more than 2 times,\\\" so that the count more accurately reflects the enemy's skill actions.\\n● Exploration\\n1. Adjusts how Multi-Layered Maps are displayed on the \\\"Map\\\" screen to prevent the layouts of unexplored areas from being revealed prematurely and affecting the gameplay experience: A Multi-Layered Map and its corresponding button now appear only after the Traveler has reached or unlocked the relevant area (before this adjustment, Multi-Layered Maps were always visible). If the corresponding area contains a tracked point, including a tracked Teleport Waypoint, the Multi-Layered Map and its button remain visible.\\n2. Optimizes the display logic when the \\\"Luna Treasure Compass\\\" and \\\"Segment-Domain Treasure Compass\\\" mark clues: Increases the display priority of Oculus icons to prevent them from being obscured by other icons. (The \\\"Cryo Treasure Compass\\\" introduced in Version 7.0 also incorporates this optimization.)\\n3. Increases the pin limit on the Map from 300 to 350.\\n● Adventurer Handbook\\n1. Optimizes the sorting logic on the \\\"Domains\\\" page of the Adventurer Handbook: All Domains are now consistently sorted based on the version in which they were added and their unlock status, with unlocked Domains from more recent versions appearing higher in the list.\\n● Inventory\\n1. Increases the combined Inventory capacity for Character Development Items, Food, Materials, Gadgets, Quest Items, and Precious Items from 2,300 to 2,600.\\n2. Increases the maximum number of Artifacts that can be stored in the Inventory from 2,400 to 2,700.\\n● Audio\\n1. Optimizes the sound effects in certain scenes, interfaces, and quests.\\n2. Optimizes Chinese and Japanese voice-over lines in certain quests.\\n● Other\\n1. Adds gyroscope support for certain Android devices that do not have a magnetometer but support a gyroscope.\\n2. Adjusts the visual effects of \\\"Stellar-Conduct\\\" and \\\"Starlight Prism\\\" when Graphics Quality is set to \\\"Low\\\" or \\\"Lowest\\\" to reduce performance load.\\n\\n〓Bug Fixes〓\\n● Quests\\n1. Fixes an issue where, sometimes under certain circumstances, the character would be teleported to an incorrect location and end up falling in an endless loop during the objective \\\"Flee from the spinning turbine\\\" in the World Quest \\\"Visitors From the Stars.\\\"\\n● Enemies\\n1. Fixes an issue where the visual effects for certain attacks performed by the enemy \\\"Ruin Hunter\\\" would display incorrectly.\\n2. Fixes an issue where the camera would behave abnormally when Sandrone used her Elemental Skill while the enemy Millennial Pearl Seahorse's Xenomare Pearl was damaged.\\n3. Fixes an issue where, under certain circumstances, the enemy \\\"Prism Slime\\\" became stuck underground when disengaging from combat, with no way to reset its state.\\n4. Fixes an issue whereby there is a chance that the enemy \\\"Moosh-Tehir\\\" behaves abnormally when using skills.\\n5. Fixes an issue whereby the enemy \\\"Precursor's Secret Source Matrix of Overseer Network\\\" is unaffected by characters' taunting skills.\\n6. Fixes an issue whereby, under certain circumstances, there is a small chance that Detection Devices deployed by the enemy \\\"Precursor's Secret Source Matrix of Overseer Network\\\" disappear unexpectedly.\\n● Characters\\n1. Fixes an issue where, when Sandrone's Charged Attack was canceled and she changed direction, some of Fagio's skill effects would also follow her new orientation in error.\\n2. Fixes an issue whereby, under certain circumstances, there is a chance that the animation for the first hit of Sandrone's Normal Attack stutters abnormally when she performs consecutive Normal Attacks.\\n3. Fixes an issue where, under certain circumstances, the Elemental RES reduction effect of Venti's Constellation 6 would sometimes not take effect.\\n4. Fixes an issue whereby, after Citlali equips the outfit \\\"Whispers of Stars and Smoke,\\\" Citlalin's movement trajectory becomes abnormal when the Jump button is held to perform a leap.\\n5. Fixes an issue whereby, following the Version Luna VIII update, there is a chance that the shield generated by Diona's Elemental Skill has an abnormal duration.\\n6. Fixes an issue whereby there is a chance that the ribbon on Aether's outfit \\\"As Heaven and Earth Are Made Anew\\\" clips through his hair.\\n7. Fixes an issue whereby there is a chance that the ribbons on Lumine's outfits \\\"As Heaven and Earth Are Made Anew\\\" and \\\"Rising Star\\\" clip through her character model.\\n8. Fixes an issue whereby, on mobile devices, certain lighting effects are missing from Lohen's Elemental Burst animation.\\n9. Fixes an issue whereby, in Co-Op Mode, when multiple Travelers are each using Yae Miko and have unlocked the Talent \\\"Edict of Cleansing,\\\" there is a chance that enhanced Sesshou Sakura lightning strikes fail to trigger the additional Electro DMG provided by the \\\"Radiance: Stellar-Conduct\\\" effect upon hitting enemies.\\n10. Fixes an issue whereby, under certain circumstances, after Cyno unlocks the Additional Talent \\\"A Star With Which to Start the Journey,\\\" there is a chance that an abnormal number of Elemental Particles are generated when his Elemental Skill hits an enemy.\\n11. Fixes an issue whereby abnormal visual effects remain in Illuga's hands after he uses his Elemental Skill by holding the Skill button.\\n● Audio\\n1. Fixes an error in the Chinese voice-over for the dialogue option \\\"How do you like it here?\\\" when interacting with Sandrone in the Serenitea Pot.\\n2. Fixes an error in a voice-over line in the Archon Quests \\\"As All Falls to Emptiness\\\" and \\\"Ancient Shadows Re-Emerge.\\\"\\n3. Fixes an issue where, following the Version \\\"Luna VIII\\\" update, the Chinese voice-over for certain lines was missing from Yelan's Travelers' Tales.\\n4. Restores certain related voice-over lines that were missing whenever Columbina performed the first hit of her Normal Attack.\\n● Miliastra Wonderland\\n1. Fixes an issue whereby, when using a keyboard and mouse on PC, there is a chance that some key inputs fail to register if multiple keys are pressed simultaneously in Miliastra Wonderland stages.\\n● Serenitea Pot\\n1. Fixes an issue where, under certain circumstances, characters would clip into the furnishing \\\"Ripples in Miniature.\\\"\\n2. Fixes an issue where the model of the furnishing \\\"Keys of Ingenuity\\\" was inconsistent with its icon and the model displayed in the \\\"Sunny Summer Fontinalia\\\" event.\\n● System\\n1. Fixes an issue whereby certain settings changes made while playing \\\"Repertoire of Myriad Melodies\\\" are not saved after logging back in.\\n2. Fixes an issue whereby character facial shading displays abnormally on the \\\"Character\\\" screen.\\n3. Fixes an issue where, under certain circumstances, the Element of the Traveler was displayed incorrectly in the \\\"Challenge Record\\\" screen during Stygian Onslaught gameplay.\\n4. Fixes an issue on mobile devices where, after using a controller to navigate from the \\\"Settings\\\" to the \\\"Pre-Install\\\" screen, players were then unable to exit the corresponding screen.\\n5. Fixes an issue in certain screens or scenes where switching to characters wearing their new outfits (specifically Citlali's \\\"Whispers of Stars and Smoke\\\" and Charlotte's \\\"Hurlock Variations\\\") might occasionally cause minor lags.\\n6. Fixes an issue in the \\\"Equipment\\\" and Weapon \\u003e Enhance screens where the weapon \\\"Ballad of the Fjords\\\" would display with an incorrect height.\\n● Other\\n1. Fixes an issue in Imaginarium Theater whereby, when the duration of certain stacks of the Brilliant Blessing \\\"Bloom: Core Condensation\\\" expires, there is a chance that all stacks are incorrectly cleared.\\n2. Fixes text errors in certain quests, interfaces, dialogues and descriptions.\\n3. Fixes an issue whereby the gadget \\\"Sandrone's Portable Tea Table\\\" can be placed inside the Knights of Favonius Headquarters when it should not be.\\n4. Fixes an issue whereby, under certain circumstances, when selecting \\\"Send Invitation\\\" while using the gadget \\\"Sandrone's Portable Tea Table,\\\" there is a chance that the \\\"Cancel Quest\\\" button is also activated.\\n5. Fixes an issue where the gadget \\\"Sandrone's Portable Tea Table\\\" could be placed while clipping through terrain and locations.\\n6. Fixes an issue whereby, on certain mobile devices or on PCs with Graphics Quality set to \\\"Low\\\" or \\\"Lowest,\\\" certain particle effects persist abnormally after Sandrone uses a Charged Attack.\\n7. Fixes some text errors in certain languages and optimizes text. (Note: Related in-game functions have not changed. Travelers can view the changes in different languages by going to the Paimon Menu \\u003e Settings \\u003e Language and changing the Game Language.)\\n◆ Optimizes inconsistencies between certain voice-overs and the corresponding lines.\\n◆ Optimizes certain English translations.\\n\\n〓Genius Invokation TCG Balance Adjustment〓\\nGenius Invokation TCG Balance Adjustment\\n1. Adjusts the number of Elemental Dice required and DMG dealt by the Elemental Skill of the Character Card \\\"Ifa\\\": The Elemental Dice cost is adjusted from 2 Anemo Dice to 3, and the DMG dealt is adjusted from 1 Anemo DMG to 2 Anemo DMG.\\n2. Adjusts the Radiant Hues enhancement effect \\\"Radiant Hues: Swift Shadow\\\" for the Elemental Skill of the Character Card \\\"Wayward Hermetic Spiritspeaker.\\\" Its effect is adjusted to: \\\"When you play Radiant Hues: Grant a random highest-cost card in your Hand Cost Reduction equal to the number of stacks of this status.\\\"\\n3. Adjusts the Elemental Skill effect of the Character Card \\\"Wayward Hermetic Spiritspeaker\\\": Effect changed to \\\"Deal 1 Cryo DMG, and place 1 Radiant Hues third from the top of your deck. If this is one of the first 4 times this skill is being used this game, then select 1 of 3 random Radiant Hues enhancement effects.\\\"\\n4. Adjusts the effects of \\\"Tonatiuh,\\\" a card generated by the Adventure effect. When Adventure Experience reaches 2, its effect is adjusted to \\\"Draw 1 card.\\\" The DMG dealt by \\\"Tide-Turning Sacred Lord\\\" is adjusted to 3 Piercing DMG.\\n5. Adjusts the effect of the Event Card \\\"In Every House a Stove\\\" when played in the first Round. Its effect is adjusted to: \\\"If your deck initially contains at least 4/2 different Talent Cards, draw 2/1 Talent Cards.\\\"\\n\\n\\n*This is a work of fiction and is not related to any actual people, events, groups, or organizations.\\n\\\"PlayStation\\\", \\\"PS5\\\", \\\"DualSense\\\", \\\"DUALSHOCK\\\" are registered trademarks or trademarks of Sony Interactive Entertainment Inc.\\n\"}]","structured_content_rows":[],"lang":"en-us","official_type":1,"reply_forbid":{"date_type":0,"start_date":"0","cur_date":"0","level":0},"video":"","contribution_id":"0","event_start_date":"0","event_end_date":"0","classification_id":"2","is_audit":false,"is_multi_language":true,"origin_lang":"en-us","sub_type":0,"reprint_source":"","can_edit":true,"last_modify_time":0,"multi_language_info":{"langs":["zh-cn","zh-tw","en-us","id-id","th-th","de-de","fr-fr","es-es","pt-pt","ru-ru","ko-kr","vi-vn","ja-jp","tr-tr","it-it"],"future_post_id":"24066","lang_subject":{"ru-ru":"Подробности обновления версии 7.0 «Безжалостный мороз»","th-th":"คำอธิบายการอัปเดตเวอร์ชัน 7.0 \"แดนหิมะที่เทวาไร้ปรานี\"","it-it":"Dettagli versione 7.0 \"Gelo spietato\"","de-de":"Erläuterungen zur Aktualisierung auf Version 7.0 „Gottverlassenes Land des Schnees“","es-es":"Detalles de la versión 7.0 «Frío eterno y cruel»","en-us":"\"Everwinter Without Mercy\" Version 7.0 Update Details","fr-fr":"Détails de la mise à jour de version 7.0 « L'impitoyable hiver éternel »","ja-jp":"Ver.7.0「神に愛されぬ雪国」正式リリース","zh-tw":"「無神憐愛的雪國」7.0版本更新說明","vi-vn":"Giới Thiệu Cập Nhật Phiên Bản 7.0 \"Đất Nước Của Tuyết Không Được Thần Thương Yêu\"","zh-cn":"「无神怜爱的雪国」7.0版本更新说明","pt-pt":"Descrição de Atualização da Versão 7.0 \"Inverno Sem Piedade\"","id-id":"Penjelasan Update Versi 7.0 \"Negeri Salju Tanpa Kasih\"","ko-kr":"「신이 사랑하지 않은 설국」 7.0 버전 업데이트 안내","tr-tr":"\"Merhametsiz Ebedi Kış\" 7.0 Sürüm Güncelleme Ayrıntıları"},"lang_content":{},"lang_structured_content":{}},"visible_level":1,"has_cover":false,"suid":"0","desc":"Dear Traveler, Below are the details of the Version 7.0 update \"Everwinter Without Mercy\" and the update compensation. 〓Compensation Details〓 Maintenance Compensation: Primogems ×300 (60 Primogems per hour the servers are down) Issue Fix Compensation: Primogems ×300 (please refer to the relevant compensation mail for more details) 〓Scope of Compensation〓 Maintenance Compensation: Travelers who have reached Adventure Rank 5 or above by 2026/08/12 06:00 (UTC+8). Compensation must be claimed before the end of Version 7.0. Issue Fix Compensation: Travelers who have reached Adventure Rank 5 or above by 2026/08/12 06:00 (UTC+8). Please log in and claim your compensation before 2026/08/15 06:00 (UTC+8). Our developers will distribute compensation to Travelers via in-game mail within 5 hours after the update maintenance is finished. The mail will expire after 30 days, so don't forget to claim the attached compensation in time. 〓Update Schedule〓 Update maintenance begins 2026/08/12 06:00 (UTC+8) and is estimated to take 5 hours. 〓How to Update Game Client〓 PC: Close the game, open the Genshin Impact Launcher, and click Update. iOS: Open the App Store and tap Update. Android: Open the game and follow the directions on-screen. PlayStation®: Highlight \"Genshin Impact\" from the Home screen, press the OPTIONS button and select \"Check for Update.\" Xbox Series X|S: Open the system main menu, select \"My games \u0026 apps,\" select the \"Manage\" tab, and on the \"Updates\" page, find \"Genshin Impact\" and confirm to update. Please do not hesitate to contact Customer Service if you encounter any issues installing the new version. We will do our very best to resolve the issue. 〓Update Details〓 I. New Areas New Region Now Available: Snezhnaya ◇ New Areas: Version 7.0 introduces the following new areas, \"Volkodlak Tundra,\" \"White Birch Snowgrave,\" \"Everfrozen Earth,\" \"Flamefeather Valley,\" and \"Fellfrost Peak\" in the Snezhnaya region. ※ Completing Archon Quest Prologue: Act III \"Song of the Dragon and Freedom\" will automatically unlock a Teleport Waypoint southwest of the Volkodlak Tundra in Snezhnaya (If you have already completed this Archon Quest, the Teleport Waypoint will be unlocked after the update). You can use this Teleport Waypoint to head over to Snezhnaya. You'll also receive the Primogem reward for this Teleport Waypoint when it unlocks automatically. ▌New System in Snezhnaya ◇ \"Meeting Points\" Cryo Sigils obtained while adventuring in the frozen expanse of Snezhnaya can be used to construct the following Meeting Points with your companions at various locations after certain other conditions have also been met: \"Tidesong Cavern,\" \"Huntsman's Cabin,\" and \"The Korolevskiy Theater.\" Then, keep raising Meeting Point Levels to earn valuable supplies. ◆ \"Huntsman's Cabin\" Unlock Criteria: • Progress through \"Gunfire in the Silent Lands\" in the Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy\" to unlock. ◆ \"Tidesong Cavern\" \u0026 \"The Korolevskiy Theater\" Unlock Criteria: • Progress through \"Silence Alone is Disfavored\" in the Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy\" to unlock. Expeditions, Daily Commissions, and other new content will also be added in Snezhnaya. ◇ Snezhnaya Daily Commissions Unlock Criteria: • Progress through \"Great Deeds on the Tundra\" in the Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy\" to unlock. Adds the Snezhnaya Fishing Association, where Travelers can exchange for new items here. In addition, there will be new Fishing Points and \"Radiant Spincrystals\" in Snezhnaya. II. New Characters \"Swirling Snow\" Odette (Cryo) (5-Star) ◇ Stellar Linchpin: Cryo ◇ Weapon: Sword ◇ A famed ballerina of Snezhnaya, she blossoms against the frozen landscape with a beauty as sharp as frost. ◆ Odette is a support character who enables the party to trigger Stellar-Conduct and Stellar Swirl reactions. She can continuously deal Stellar Glimmer DMG (Stellar-Conduct/Stellar Swirl) from off-field, provide consistent Cryo application, and increase the party's Stellar Glimmer DMG. Traveler (Cryo) (5-Star) ◆ After resonating with Cryo, the Traveler enables the party to trigger Stellar Glimmer (Stellar-Conduct/Stellar Swirl). They can deal damage from off-field and in quick-swap rotations, and can also serve as an on-field DPS while in the \"Radiance: Stellar-Conduct\" state. \"Swift-Striding Hound\" Alyosha (Electro) (4-Star) ◇ Vision: Electro ◇ Weapon: Polearm ◇ A \"professional hunter\" mastering the Snezhnayan snowfields. Beneath his calm demeanor, a fiercely distinct \"ideal\" seems to burn. ◆ Alyosha is a support character who heals party members while continuously dealing Electro DMG. III. New Equipment 1. Event-Exclusive Weapon Whitelake Frostfeather (5-Star Sword) Whitelake Frostfeather (Sword) greatly boosts ATK and Stellar Glimmer CRIT DMG, while also restoring Elemental Energy. ◆ The event-exclusive 5-star weapon Whitelake Frostfeather (Sword) can be obtained from the Event Wish. Please refer to the relevant official Event Notices for specific acquisition details. 2. Special Weapon Exaiphanes Blade (5-Star Sword) Exaiphanes Blade (Sword) greatly boosts the Traveler's ATK and restores Elemental Energy upon hitting an opponent. ◆ Exaiphanes Blade (Sword) can be obtained by progressing through \"Great Deeds on the Tundra\" in Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy.\" ◆ You can enhance your Exaiphanes Blade after using Cryo to awaken and connect to the Statues of The Seven in Snezhnaya. 3. Forgeable Weapons New Forgeable Weapons (4-Star) Emberwell (Sword): Triggering an Elemental Reaction increases ATK, and triggering a Stellar Glimmer Reaction increases Stellar Glimmer DMG. Blade of Atonement (Claymore): Triggering an Elemental Reaction increases Elemental Mastery, and triggering a Stellar Glimmer Reaction increases ATK. Song of the Vigil (Polearm): Triggering an Elemental Reaction restores Elemental Energy, and triggering a Stellar Glimmer Reaction increases ATK. Echoes of the Heart (Catalyst): Triggering an Elemental Reaction increases Elemental Mastery, and triggering a Stellar Glimmer Reaction increases Stellar Glimmer DMG. Covenant of Frost and Snow (Bow): Increases Elemental Mastery when the equipping character uses an Elemental Skill. ◆ You can exchange for Weapon Forging Blueprints from Kuzmichev in Snezhnograd of Snezhnaya by consuming certain amounts and types of materials. 4. Battle Pass Weapons New Battle Pass Weapons (4-Star) Heretic's Molten Blade (Sword): Grants an ATK bonus after the equipping character uses an Elemental Skill. The bonus increases based on the distance they travel. Forged by the Golden Melody (Claymore): Successively grants bonuses to ATK, Elemental Mastery, and Stellar Glimmer DMG. Frostbreath (Polearm): grants an ATK bonus when the equipping character triggers a Cryo- or Hydro-related reaction, while also restoring Elemental Energy to party members. Clash of Kings (Catalyst): Increases ATK and Elemental Mastery when the equipping character uses an Elemental Skill. Jade Vista (Bow): Grants either an Elemental Mastery or ATK bonus depending on whether other party members share the equipping character's Elemental Type. ◆ 5 new weapons will be added to the BP Bounty. After unlocking the Gnostic Hymn and reaching Level 30, Travelers can select 1 weapon from a total of 15 as a reward. 5. New Artifact Sets Scarlet Proof (4-Star and 5-Star) ◇ 2-Piece Set: ATK +18%. ◇ 4-Piece Set: Increases the equipping character's CRIT Rate by 16%, and their Stellar Swirl reaction dealt by 40%, for 10s after they trigger a Stellar Swirl reaction. Heart of the Furnace (4-Star and 5-Star) ◇ 2-Piece Set: ATK +18%. ◇ 4-Piece Set: Increases the equipping character's ATK by 12% for 12s when they trigger a Stellar Glimmer reaction or deal Stellar Glimmer reaction DMG. Also increases Stellar Glimmer reaction DMG dealt by all nearby party members by 50%. The above effects can trigger even when the equipping character is not on the field, and the DMG bonus from multiple Artifact Sets with the same name does not stack. How to Obtain: Challenge the new Domain of Blessing in Everfrozen Earth, Snezhnaya, \"Inverted Glacier.\" IV. New Main Story 1. New Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I - Everwinter Without Mercy Permanently available after the Version 7.0 update ◆ Quest Unlock Criteria: • Adventure Rank 18 or above • Complete the Archon Quest \"Prologue: Act III - Song of the Dragon and Freedom\" • The \"Focused Experience Mode\" function is available for this quest. Chapter VII: Act II - Wraith's Nocturne Permanently available after the Version 7.0 update ◆ Quest Unlock Criteria: • Adventure Rank 18 or above • Complete Chapter VII: Act I - \"Everwinter Without Mercy\" • The \"Focused Experience Mode\" function is available for this quest. ※ Travelers who meet the unlock requirements can use the automatically unlocked Teleport Waypoint to reach Snezhnaya and begin Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy\" even if they have not completed the preceding Archon Quests, such as \"Song of the Welkin Moon: Act X.\" 2. New World Quests New World Quests \"Hesperides of Love and Hate\" Quest Chain, \"In the Dwelling of Life\" Quest Chain, \"On One Side a Palace, On the Other a Tomb\" Quest Chain, \"Her Palace Collapses Into the Blizzard\" Quest Chain, \"Mean Streets of the Despicable\" Quest Chain, \"The Soft Song She Sang\" Quest Chain, \"In the Tranquility of Cycles\" Quest Chain, \"Small Jack Frost, Big Problems,\" \"Forested Snowfield,\" \"For an Ice Mirror Fragment,\" and more. ※ Progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy\" and complete \"Gunfire in the Silent Lands\" to unlock these quests. V. Elemental Reaction New Stellar Glimmer Reaction: Stellar Swirl Under certain conditions, Anemo and Cryo can trigger Stellar Swirl, dealing one instance of Anemo DMG to the target and creating a Stellar Vortex. Only one Stellar Vortex can exist within the same area at a time. A Stellar Vortex detonates after a short delay, dealing AoE Cryo DMG. Triggering Stellar Swirl nearby a certain number of times increases the vortex's level, expanding its blast radius and increasing its DMG. Triggering additional Stellar Swirl reactions nearby can also cause the vortex to detonate early. The aforementioned DMG can trigger CRIT Hits. When the Stellar Vortex explodes, it will also grant nearby characters the ability to jump higher once, for a short time. Additionally, triggering Stellar Swirl grants certain nearby characters the \"Radiance: Stellar Swirl\" effect, enhancing some of their Talents and skill effects. Certain characters can also utilize their Talents to deal Stellar Swirl DMG to enemies. This DMG can trigger CRIT Hits. VI. New Enemies Immortal Construct ◇ A nigh-immortal life form created through bio-alchemy. The Immortal Construct burns its life to enter the \"Lifeflare\" state, in which it gains several HP shields at one time. Any DMG dealt by it while in this state will restore its HP. When the number of HP-restoring shields goes below a certain number or after Lifeflare lasts for a set time, the Immortal Construct will attempt to unleash \"Scorching Radiance.\" To stop it, you must break all of its HP shields. The Immortal Construct will be unable to recover any HP when affected by Stellar Glimmer reactions, no matter what it does... Located in Everfrozen Earth Chimeric Winged Lion ◇ A product of bio-alchemy, and one of the flawed artificial monsters cast aside in pursuit of a certain grand ambition. The Chimeric Winged Lion will oscillate between two enhanced states: \"Thundercall\" and \"Galeforce.\" When it is in the Thundercall state, it will become weakened when its Elemental Ward is broken. Additionally, any attempts by it to spread its thunder blades can be disrupted by the Stellar Glimmer reaction. When it is in the Galeforce state, it will attempt to absorb any Anemo Orbs that are on the field to charge its attack. At this time, destroying the orbs or using the Stellar Glimmer reaction can stop its charging and weaken it. Located in Volkodlak Tundra Wildwood Leshy Rugged Elder Leshy, Juvenile Tree Segment ◇ A species of Snezhnayan fae, these tree spirits inhabit the forests and wilds. Certain aspects of their behavior can be disrupted by the Stellar Glimmer Reaction. Volkodlak Brute Voywolf Hunter, Fanged Zealot, Leomastiff Guard, Channel Contact, Long-Eared Striker, Volkodlak Raider, Volkodlak Sharpshooter, Volkodlak Basher, Volkodlak Lobber ◇ A species of Snezhnayan fae, the Volkodlak comprise numerous distinct clans. Certain aspects of their behavior can be disrupted by the Stellar Glimmer Reaction. Aberrant Chimeric Monsters Chimeric Horned Bear, Chimeric Burrowbeast, Chimeric Armored Beast, Chimeric Winged Elephant ◇ A product of bio-alchemy that was once widespread across the frozen lands, an aberrant chimeric monster. Certain aspects of their behavior can be disrupted by the Stellar Glimmer Reaction. Other Fae Glacial Warden, Glaciomancer ◇ A species of Snezhnayan fae, Snegoviks live for love amid the snow and ice. While in certain states, they become susceptible to disruption from the Stellar Glimmer Reaction. Winged Halberd-Knight, Winged Soarer Knight ◇ A species of Snezhnayan fae, these winged Vila can fly. Certain aspects of their behavior can be disrupted by the Stellar Glimmer Reaction. VII. New Domains Domain of Forgery: Scars of Cursed Obsession ◇ Challenge the Domain to obtain Weapon Ascension Materials. ◇ Unlock Criteria (satisfy any one of the criteria below to unlock): • Reach Adventure Rank 10 or above • Complete \"Knights of Favonius\" in Archon Quest Prologue: Act I \"The Outlander Who Caught the Wind\" Domain of Mastery: Relics of the Fallen Grace ◇ Challenge the Domain to obtain Character Talent Materials. ◇ Unlock Criteria (satisfy any one of the criteria below to unlock): • Reach Adventure Rank 10 or above • Complete \"Knights of Favonius\" in Archon Quest Prologue: Act I \"The Outlander Who Caught the Wind\" Domain of Blessing: Inverted Glacier ◇ Challenge the Domain to obtain artifacts in the \"Scarlet Proof\" and \"Heart of the Furnace\" sets. ◇ Unlock Criteria (satisfy any one of the criteria below to unlock): • Reach Adventure Rank 10 or above • Complete \"Knights of Favonius\" in Archon Quest Prologue: Act I \"The Outlander Who Caught the Wind\" VIII. System Update 1. New Items Eye of Graeae ◇ A strange mechanism you encountered in an abandoned station in Snezhnaya. It often appears in the form of a monocle. The Eye of Graeae provides a variety of convenient functions. Travelers can use it to call a train and travel between cities, craft items or claim Daily Commission rewards while aboard, and create various Prime Ice Constructs to assist with exploration and adventuring. ◆ Unlock Criteria • Unlocks as you progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy.\" 2. New Gameplay Third-Person Shooter Combat Gameplay Use a variety of firearms and equipment to defeat opponents through Elemental Reactions in the Shadow Realm. As you progress through your adventure and unlock new gameplay, you will gain access to a variety of firearms and equipment. ◆ Unlock Criteria • This combat gameplay mode becomes available as you progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy.\" ▌ After unlocking the Third-Person Shooter Combat Gameplay, Travelers can take part in the associated \"Special Recruitment Project: Cycle Training\" to obtain rewards. ◇ Each week, you can accept new Training Quests from Yarovaya, in which you are tasked with entering and cleaning up specific Shadow Realms. Complete a certain number of these weekly quests to obtain various rewards. ◆ Unlock Criteria • Progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act II \"Wraith's Nocturne\" to unlock the prerequisite quest. Complete that quest to gain access to this feature. ▌ At the shooting range onboard the train, you can undertake special challenges at the simulated Shadow Realm \"Edge of Survival.\" This is where you can push your enemy-clearing skills to the limit and sharpen your proficiency with firearms. More \"Edge of Survival\" stages will be added in future versions. Each \"Edge of Survival\" challenge stage has its own Frontrunners' Edge section with \"All Records\" and \"Friends' Records\" tabs, allowing Travelers to view the challenge results of other Travelers and their friends. *The \"All Records\" tab becomes available on August 17 once data compilation is complete. Prime Ice Construct Travelers can use the Eye of Graeae to create a variety of Prime Ice Constructs throughout the open world. Prime Ice Constructs can aid in exploration in the open world and allow Travelers to leave behind messages and materials to assist those in other worlds. While exploring Snezhnaya, Travelers may come across Prime Ice Constructs created by other Travelers. These constructs can help make exploration easier. Additionally, Travelers can also give a Like to any Prime Ice Constructs they find helpful, while their own constructs may likewise receive Likes when they assist Travelers in other worlds. ◆ Unlock Criteria • Progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy\" and complete \"Gunfire in the Silent Lands\" to unlock this feature. 3. New System Snezhnaya Adventure Journal ◇ The Snezhnaya Adventure Journal records your progress through adventures in Snezhnaya, along with content yet to be explored and rewards waiting to be claimed. You can use it as a one-stop overview of what remains to be explored in Snezhnaya and to track the relevant quests. ◆ Unlock Criteria • Progress through Archon Quest Chapter VII: Act I \"Everwinter Without Mercy\" and complete \"Gunfire in the Silent Lands\" to unlock this feature. 4. Gameplay Update Stellar-Conduct: \"Starlight Prism\" — Open-World Interaction Update In certain places in Snezhnaya, a Starlight Prism will also generate a Prism Mirage that lasts for a short time at the same location when it vanishes. Approach the mirage to activate the Starlight Prism again, at which point it will remain on the field permanently. Prisms activated by such interactions have a chance to appear in other Travelers' worlds. Similarly, Prisms from other Travelers' worlds may also appear in your world. Within the Polestar Field created by a Starlight Prism, the Eye of Graeae's energy will not deplete and will remain at or above 30%. Prime Ice Constructs inside a Polestar Field will gain various wondrous buffs. IX. Miliastra Wonderland Miliastra Wonderland Update ◆ Cosmetic Sets The \"Phantasmagoric Discourse\" Event Ode brings 4 new sets: \"Whimsical Spectacle,\" \"Azure Mountainshade,\" \"Sleuth's Verdict,\" and \"Twilight Phantom Thief.\" \"Chronicles of the Realms\"/\"Epic of the Realms\" features 3 new sets: \"Letter Crane Courier,\" \"Scary Cat,\" and \"Precision Strike.\" Available for a limited time only from the Miliastra Shop: 3 new sets. They are \"Cloudbound Journey/Cloudbound Flight,\" \"Fun Under Open Skies,\" and \"Warrior of the Winning Hand.\" \"Encounter Echoes\" Standard Ode: 1 new Set Catalog, \"Crowned by the Breeze,\" is available. Take part in the \"Raiment Collection: Gentle Warmth\" event to obtain the new \"Amber Nectar\" set. After the version update, the set \"Dreamy Summer Leisure\" that was obtainable through an earlier limited-time event will be available for a limited time at the Miliastra Shop. ◆ Lobby With the new version update, the Public Lobby will be changed to a new theme: \"Miracle Theater: Dreamcraft.\" Travelers can purchase the new Private Lobby \"Miracle Theater: Light and Shadow Spectacle\" through the Miliastra Pass. ◆ Wonderlands Adds the \"Wonderland Rising Stars\" section, which showcases the latest creations and updates from Craftspeople. Adds the \"Wonderland Topic\" section, featuring regularly updated selections of Wonderland stages curated around specific themes. Adds replies to stage comments. Comments now show how long the commenter had played the stage when posting, as well as whether the stage was in Early Access at the time. The stage details page now displays the stage's recommendation rate over the past 30 days, calculated from comments posted during that period. The new version also adds additional cosmetic components, expressions, and special effects. For updates regarding the \"Miliastra Wonderland\" stage editor and Miliastra Sandbox, Travelers can check \"My Miliastra Wonderland\" \u003e \"Notices.\" X. Genius Invokation TCG Genius Invokation TCG Gameplay Update New Character Card: Durin, Jahoda, and their corresponding Talent cards. Corresponding invitation duel and guest challenges have been added to the Player List. New Character Card: Hydro Hypostasis and the corresponding Talent card. The Tavern Challenge has also been added. New Action Cards \"Witch's Homework,\" \"Feasting in a Shared Toast,\" \"Temporal Wind's Eulogy,\" \"Phantasmal Nocturne,\" \"Genesis of Starsigns,\" and \"Sparkborne Magic\" have been added, which can be purchased from Prince at The Cat's Tail. New Card Back \"Snezhnaya\" can be purchased from Prince at The Cat's Tail after reaching the corresponding Player Level. The Forge Realm's Temper is once again available. The theme of this edition is \"The Forge Realm's Temper: Game of Wits\": (1) During The Forge Realm's Temper: Game of Wits, some stages will have special victory and defeat conditions or unique Special Rules. Adeptly adapt your tactics to complete the challenge and avoid the conditions for defeat! (2) Within The Forge Realm's Temper: Game of Wits event stages, there will also be special victory or defeat rules that can easily exert influence on the tempo of the match. Fully utilizing these special rules will contribute greatly to your success. XI. Imaginarium Theater Update Scheduled for September 1 After the Version 7.0 update, a new season of Imaginarium Theater will be available on September 1, 2026. Required Elemental Types: Hydro, Electro, and Dendro Opening Characters: Columbina, Xingqiu, Cyno, Kuki Shinobu, Lauma, and Kaveh When Imaginarium Theater is open, the corresponding Opening Characters will obtain Fantastical Blessings. Special Guest Stars: Odette, Sandrone, Sucrose, and Nicole After the new season of Imaginarium Theater begins, the characters Flins, Columbina, Kirara, and Illuga will each gain a new \"Thespian Trick\" that can be exchanged from the NPC Wolfy. Envisaged Echoes Update After the Version 7.0 update, new challenge stages and Echo cosmetics for Tartaglia and Xiao will be added. XII. Spiral Abyss Update Scheduled for August 16 ◇ After the Version 7.0 update, Phase 1 of the Spiral Abyss will be updated on August 16. ◆ Floor 9 Ley Line Disorder changed to: Characters' Stellar Swirl DMG increased by 50%. ◆ Floor 10 Ley Line Disorder changed to: Characters' Stellar-Conduct DMG increased by 50%. ◆ Floor 11 Ley Line Disorder changed to: All party members receive a 60% Cryo DMG Bonus. All party members gain a 60% Pyro DMG Bonus. ◆ Floor 12 Ley Line Disorders changed to: First Half: Characters' Superconduct DMG increased by 200% and Stellar-Conduct DMG increased by 75%. Second Half: Characters' Normal Attack Pyro DMG increased by 75%. ◆ Updated the monster lineup on Floors 9, 10, 11, and 12 of the Spiral Abyss. ◆ Blessing of the Abyssal Moon: Luster-Piercing Moon While the active character is inside a Polestar Field, when they deal DMG to opponents, their attacks will unleash a shockwave at the opponent's position that deals True DMG. This can trigger once every 4s. ◇ Starting from this edition of Spiral Abyss, the \"Disenchantment in Deep Shadow\" and \"Celestial Gift\" Artifact set rewards in Domain Reliquary: Tier I and Domain Reliquary: Tier II obtained from the Ley Lines on Floors 9–12 will be replaced with the \"Scarlet Proof\" and the \"Heart of the Furnace\" sets. Update Scheduled for September 16 ◇ After the Version 7.0 update, Phase 2 of the Spiral Abyss will be updated on September 16. ◆ Floor 11 Ley Line Disorder changed to: All party members gain a 60% Anemo DMG Bonus. All party members gain a 60% Electro DMG Bonus. ◆ Floor 12 Ley Line Disorders changed to: First Half: Characters' Swirl DMG increased by 200% and Stellar Swirl DMG increased by 75%. Second Half: Characters' Electro-Charged DMG increased by 200% and Lunar-Charged DMG increased by 75%. ◆ Updated the monster lineup on Floors 11 – 12 of the Spiral Abyss. ◆ Blessing of the Abyssal Moon: Cascading Moon When a character deals Swirl or Stellar Swirl DMG to an opponent, a shockwave will be unleashed at the opponent's position, dealing True DMG. This effect can be triggered once every 4s. XIII. Other Update Details 1. New Recipe: ○ Exploration or Quest Rewards: \"Glupov Rye Bread,\" \"Stroganina,\" \"Rimecurrant Ice Creams,\" \"Snowball Blooms Atop Snowfields,\" and \"Snowrealm Okroshkas.\" ○ From Snezhnaya NPC Buturlina: \"Podvorye Smoked Sausage,\" \"Borscht,\" and \"Medovik.\" ○ From Snezhnaya NPC Tolstaya: \"Zharkoye\" and \"Snezhnaya Shashliks.\" 2. New Character Specialty Dishes: ○ Alyosha's specialty: \"The Bullseye Roast\" ○ Odette's specialty: Lakeside Snow Swan 3. Adds the \"Snezhnaya: Sacred City of Ice and Pale Star (I),\" \"Land of Surging Shadows,\" \"Meetings in Outrealm: Series VII,\" and \"Mortal Travails: Series VII\" Achievement categories, as well as new Achievements to the \"Wonders of the World\" category. 4. Adds Set 51 of \"Paimon's Paintings\" chat emojis. 5. Adds some prompts for loading screens. 6. New Namecards: \"Odette: The Singular Swan\": Reward for reaching Friendship Lv. 10 with Odette \"Alyosha: Sit\": Reward for reaching Friendship Lv. 10 with Alyosha \"Achievement: Resplendence\": Reward for completing all achievements under \"Meetings in Outrealm: Series VII\" \"Snezhnaya: Long Night\": Reward for completing all achievements under \"Snezhnaya: Sacred City of Ice and Pale Star (I)\" \"Achievement: Treading Snow\": Reward for completing all achievements under \"Mortal Travails: Series VII\" \"Snezhnaya: Fleeting Glimpses\": Reward for completing all Special Recruitment Project: Cycle Training quests \"Achievement: Enigmatic Core\": Reward for completing all achievements under \"Land of Surging Shadows\" \"Travel Notes: Frostfarer\": Reward obtained via the BP system 7. Another 2 sets of Artifacts are available to exchange in the Mystic Offering system: Night of the Sky's Unveiling and Silken Moon's Serenade. 8. Adds new Wildlife: Nochhornowl, Red-Bellied Plover, Fuzzbadger, Severelk, Polyarbear, Fluffahog, Morozhound, White Sumpter Beast, Ledobug, and Kristall Bug. You can use the Omni-Ubiquity Net to capture certain wildlife species found in Snezhnaya. 9. Adds new Fish: Charcoal Snowfin, Cream Snowfin, Moonlight Snowfin, Ruby Starbloom Fish, Frostpetal Starbloom Fish, and Iridescent Starbloom Fish. 10. Adds some of the Harvestable seeds from Snezhnaya to the Seed Dispensary. 11. Adds Series II of \"Valiant Chronicles,\" featuring 3 new Local Legends and the corresponding challenges introduced in this version: Bandersnatch, Churin, and Furiosa. Complete the required number of challenges to obtain the \"First Snow\" avatar frame. 12. The August 10, 2026 update to \"To Temper Thyself and Journey Far\" expands the selection of available Stella Fortuna, adding Stella Fortuna for the following characters: Lyney, Wriothesley, Navia, Xianyun, Chiori, Sigewinne, Clorinde, Emilie, and Yumemizuki Mizuki. After the Version 7.0 update, \"Long-Term Encounter Points\" will be reset. Travelers, please take note. 〓Adjustments \u0026 Optimizations〓 ● Quests 1. Adds a teleportation function for quest objectives: Some quest objective locations now support teleportation. Select a supported objective on the \"Map\" screen and click the \"Go\" button to teleport to the quest objective or a nearby location. (This feature initially applies to certain quests in the Version 7.0 update. Future versions expand support to more new quests and further optimize the feature.) ● Enemies 1. Optimizes how attempts are counted for the related \"Valiant Chronicles\" challenge objective to: \"Before the Prism Slime first gathers light and swells, make sure it attempts to absorb energy no more than 2 times,\" so that the count more accurately reflects the enemy's skill actions. ● Exploration 1. Adjusts how Multi-Layered Maps are displayed on the \"Map\" screen to prevent the layouts of unexplored areas from being revealed prematurely and affecting the gameplay experience: A Multi-Layered Map and its corresponding button now appear only after the Traveler has reached or unlocked the relevant area (before this adjustment, Multi-Layered Maps were always visible). If the corresponding area contains a tracked point, including a tracked Teleport Waypoint, the Multi-Layered Map and its button remain visible. 2. Optimizes the display logic when the \"Luna Treasure Compass\" and \"Segment-Domain Treasure Compass\" mark clues: Increases the display priority of Oculus icons to prevent them from being obscured by other icons. (The \"Cryo Treasure Compass\" introduced in Version 7.0 also incorporates this optimization.) 3. Increases the pin limit on the Map from 300 to 350. ● Adventurer Handbook 1. Optimizes the sorting logic on the \"Domains\" page of the Adventurer Handbook: All Domains are now consistently sorted based on the version in which they were added and their unlock status, with unlocked Domains from more recent versions appearing higher in the list. ● Inventory 1. Increases the combined Inventory capacity for Character Development Items, Food, Materials, Gadgets, Quest Items, and Precious Items from 2,300 to 2,600. 2. Increases the maximum number of Artifacts that can be stored in the Inventory from 2,400 to 2,700. ● Audio 1. Optimizes the sound effects in certain scenes, interfaces, and quests. 2. Optimizes Chinese and Japanese voice-over lines in certain quests. ● Other 1. Adds gyroscope support for certain Android devices that do not have a magnetometer but support a gyroscope. 2. Adjusts the visual effects of \"Stellar-Conduct\" and \"Starlight Prism\" when Graphics Quality is set to \"Low\" or \"Lowest\" to reduce performance load. 〓Bug Fixes〓 ● Quests 1. Fixes an issue where, sometimes under certain circumstances, the character would be teleported to an incorrect location and end up falling in an endless loop during the objective \"Flee from the spinning turbine\" in the World Quest \"Visitors From the Stars.\" ● Enemies 1. Fixes an issue where the visual effects for certain attacks performed by the enemy \"Ruin Hunter\" would display incorrectly. 2. Fixes an issue where the camera would behave abnormally when Sandrone used her Elemental Skill while the enemy Millennial Pearl Seahorse's Xenomare Pearl was damaged. 3. Fixes an issue where, under certain circumstances, the enemy \"Prism Slime\" became stuck underground when disengaging from combat, with no way to reset its state. 4. Fixes an issue whereby there is a chance that the enemy \"Moosh-Tehir\" behaves abnormally when using skills. 5. Fixes an issue whereby the enemy \"Precursor's Secret Source Matrix of Overseer Network\" is unaffected by characters' taunting skills. 6. Fixes an issue whereby, under certain circumstances, there is a small chance that Detection Devices deployed by the enemy \"Precursor's Secret Source Matrix of Overseer Network\" disappear unexpectedly. ● Characters 1. Fixes an issue where, when Sandrone's Charged Attack was canceled and she changed direction, some of Fagio's skill effects would also follow her new orientation in error. 2. Fixes an issue whereby, under certain circumstances, there is a chance that the animation for the first hit of Sandrone's Normal Attack stutters abnormally when she performs consecutive Normal Attacks. 3. Fixes an issue where, under certain circumstances, the Elemental RES reduction effect of Venti's Constellation 6 would sometimes not take effect. 4. Fixes an issue whereby, after Citlali equips the outfit \"Whispers of Stars and Smoke,\" Citlalin's movement trajectory becomes abnormal when the Jump button is held to perform a leap. 5. Fixes an issue whereby, following the Version Luna VIII update, there is a chance that the shield generated by Diona's Elemental Skill has an abnormal duration. 6. Fixes an issue whereby there is a chance that the ribbon on Aether's outfit \"As Heaven and Earth Are Made Anew\" clips through his hair. 7. Fixes an issue whereby there is a chance that the ribbons on Lumine's outfits \"As Heaven and Earth Are Made Anew\" and \"Rising Star\" clip through her character model. 8. Fixes an issue whereby, on mobile devices, certain lighting effects are missing from Lohen's Elemental Burst animation. 9. Fixes an issue whereby, in Co-Op Mode, when multiple Travelers are each using Yae Miko and have unlocked the Talent \"Edict of Cleansing,\" there is a chance that enhanced Sesshou Sakura lightning strikes fail to trigger the additional Electro DMG provided by the \"Radiance: Stellar-Conduct\" effect upon hitting enemies. 10. Fixes an issue whereby, under certain circumstances, after Cyno unlocks the Additional Talent \"A Star With Which to Start the Journey,\" there is a chance that an abnormal number of Elemental Particles are generated when his Elemental Skill hits an enemy. 11. Fixes an issue whereby abnormal visual effects remain in Illuga's hands after he uses his Elemental Skill by holding the Skill button. ● Audio 1. Fixes an error in the Chinese voice-over for the dialogue option \"How do you like it here?\" when interacting with Sandrone in the Serenitea Pot. 2. Fixes an error in a voice-over line in the Archon Quests \"As All Falls to Emptiness\" and \"Ancient Shadows Re-Emerge.\" 3. Fixes an issue where, following the Version \"Luna VIII\" update, the Chinese voice-over for certain lines was missing from Yelan's Travelers' Tales. 4. Restores certain related voice-over lines that were missing whenever Columbina performed the first hit of her Normal Attack. ● Miliastra Wonderland 1. Fixes an issue whereby, when using a keyboard and mouse on PC, there is a chance that some key inputs fail to register if multiple keys are pressed simultaneously in Miliastra Wonderland stages. ● Serenitea Pot 1. Fixes an issue where, under certain circumstances, characters would clip into the furnishing \"Ripples in Miniature.\" 2. Fixes an issue where the model of the furnishing \"Keys of Ingenuity\" was inconsistent with its icon and the model displayed in the \"Sunny Summer Fontinalia\" event. ● System 1. Fixes an issue whereby certain settings changes made while playing \"Repertoire of Myriad Melodies\" are not saved after logging back in. 2. Fixes an issue whereby character facial shading displays abnormally on the \"Character\" screen. 3. Fixes an issue where, under certain circumstances, the Element of the Traveler was displayed incorrectly in the \"Challenge Record\" screen during Stygian Onslaught gameplay. 4. Fixes an issue on mobile devices where, after using a controller to navigate from the \"Settings\" to the \"Pre-Install\" screen, players were then unable to exit the corresponding screen. 5. Fixes an issue in certain screens or scenes where switching to characters wearing their new outfits (specifically Citlali's \"Whispers of Stars and Smoke\" and Charlotte's \"Hurlock Variations\") might occasionally cause minor lags. 6. Fixes an issue in the \"Equipment\" and Weapon \u003e Enhance screens where the weapon \"Ballad of the Fjords\" would display with an incorrect height. ● Other 1. Fixes an issue in Imaginarium Theater whereby, when the duration of certain stacks of the Brilliant Blessing \"Bloom: Core Condensation\" expires, there is a chance that all stacks are incorrectly cleared. 2. Fixes text errors in certain quests, interfaces, dialogues and descriptions. 3. Fixes an issue whereby the gadget \"Sandrone's Portable Tea Table\" can be placed inside the Knights of Favonius Headquarters when it should not be. 4. Fixes an issue whereby, under certain circumstances, when selecting \"Send Invitation\" while using the gadget \"Sandrone's Portable Tea Table,\" there is a chance that the \"Cancel Quest\" button is also activated. 5. Fixes an issue where the gadget \"Sandrone's Portable Tea Table\" could be placed while clipping through terrain and locations. 6. Fixes an issue whereby, on certain mobile devices or on PCs with Graphics Quality set to \"Low\" or \"Lowest,\" certain particle effects persist abnormally after Sandrone uses a Charged Attack. 7. Fixes some text errors in certain languages and optimizes text. (Note: Related in-game functions have not changed. Travelers can view the changes in different languages by going to the Paimon Menu \u003e Settings \u003e Language and changing the Game Language.) ◆ Optimizes inconsistencies between certain voice-overs and the corresponding lines. ◆ Optimizes certain English translations. 〓Genius Invokation TCG Balance Adjustment〓 Genius Invokation TCG Balance Adjustment 1. Adjusts the number of Elemental Dice required and DMG dealt by the Elemental Skill of the Character Card \"Ifa\": The Elemental Dice cost is adjusted from 2 Anemo Dice to 3, and the DMG dealt is adjusted from 1 Anemo DMG to 2 Anemo DMG. 2. Adjusts the Radiant Hues enhancement effect \"Radiant Hues: Swift Shadow\" for the Elemental Skill of the Character Card \"Wayward Hermetic Spiritspeaker.\" Its effect is adjusted to: \"When you play Radiant Hues: Grant a random highest-cost card in your Hand Cost Reduction equal to the number of stacks of this status.\" 3. Adjusts the Elemental Skill effect of the Character Card \"Wayward Hermetic Spiritspeaker\": Effect changed to \"Deal 1 Cryo DMG, and place 1 Radiant Hues third from the top of your deck. If this is one of the first 4 times this skill is being used this game, then select 1 of 3 random Radiant Hues enhancement effects.\" 4. Adjusts the effects of \"Tonatiuh,\" a card generated by the Adventure effect. When Adventure Experience reaches 2, its effect is adjusted to \"Draw 1 card.\" The DMG dealt by \"Tide-Turning Sacred Lord\" is adjusted to 3 Piercing DMG. 5. Adjusts the effect of the Event Card \"In Every House a Stove\" when played in the first Round. Its effect is adjusted to: \"If your deck initially contains at least 4/2 different Talent Cards, draw 2/1 Talent Cards.\" *This is a work of fiction and is not related to any actual people, events, groups, or organizations. \"PlayStation\", \"PS5\", \"DualSense\", \"DUALSHOCK\" are registered trademarks or trademarks of Sony Interactive Entertainment Inc.","game_uid":"0","game_region":"","channel_id":"28"},"forum":null,"topics":[],"user":{"uid":"1015537","nickname":"Genshin Impact Official","introduce":"Grand Master of Genshin Impact Forum","avatar":"100236","gender":0,"certification":{"type":1,"icon_url":"https://hyl-static-res-prod.hoyolab.com/upload/static-resource/2022/02/23/f5a37763f0f2080c0c43cca8638af024_5295925290813405198.webp","desc":"Official Big Boss"},"level_exp":{"level":0,"exp":0},"is_following":false,"is_followed":false,"avatar_url":"https://fastcdn.hoyoverse.com/static-resource-v2/2024/04/10/71a62b9a993534f3db7896fc6f725ff8_4436020059642725994.webp","auth":null,"is_logoff":false,"pendant":"","was_following":false,"post_num":4542,"suid":"0","black_relation":{"is_blacking":false,"is_blacked":false},"badge":null,"lantern":null,"otaku_devotion_title":{"icon":"","name":"","desc":"","otaku_identity":"OtakuIdentityNone","accompany_title":"AccompanyTitleUnknown","role_id":"0"},"allow_community":true,"content_cannot_be_upvoted":false,"content_cannot_be_replied":false,"post_cannot_be_shared":false,"post_cannot_be_collected":false,"cannot_be_followed":false},"self_operation":{"attitude":0,"is_collected":false},"stat":{"view_num":89642,"reply_num":368,"like_num":2787,"bookmark_num":239,"share_num":50,"view_num_unit":"","reply_num_unit":"","like_num_unit":"","bookmark_num_unit":"","share_num_unit":"","true_view_num":0,"click_view_num":0,"summary_for_creator":null,"multi_upvote_stats":[{"upvote_id":"1","upvote_num":2661},{"upvote_id":"4